{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals","id":812137,"title":"Ex3 Thaumaturgy Rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T14:47:53-08:00","id":812137,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ex3 Thaumaturgy Rituals","content":"The Ex3 book doesn't have too many Thaumaturgy Rituals and the ones there seem to imply a mortal only knowing a single ritual. Anyone have any ideas for other rituals? <br /> <br /> I'm mostly looking for medicine or warding type rituals. All the ones I think of seem to mirror Medicine Charms which is too overpowered for the character. The character I need it for is an NPC with little chance of Exalting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:31:31-08:00","id":812240,"title":"","content":"So, I've been thinking a bit more about this and came up with a few healing Rituals. The idea is to limit them to fixing symptoms instead of healing the disease. I'm hoping they don't overlap with what you can do with the medicine ability.<ul><li>Herbal Smoke to suppress coughing</li> <li>Cloth to place on forehead to bring down fever</li> <li>Powder to instantly kill headaches.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:37:51-08:00","id":812247,"title":"","content":"Those sound more like basic applications of Medicine to me.<br /> <br /> In penance for being a wet blanket, I'll try to think some stuff up. I'll get back to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:39:41-08:00","id":812248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=812247#post812247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sound more like basic applications of Medicine to me.<br /> <br /> In penance for being a wet blanket, I'll try to think some stuff up. I'll get back to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is what I was afraid of. It's hard to think of a happy medium between Charm Healing and &quot;eat this herb and call me in the morning&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:48:03-08:00","id":812278,"title":"","content":"A way to boil an egg. open it up and get a accuratish fortune cookie fortune.<br /> <br /> Turn water into Wine.<br /> <br /> Pick up a Y shaped stick and find stuff, you know...dowsing.<br /> <br /> Crush up some pearls. put it in water. say some weird prayers. sprinkle that on graves to stop ghosts from showing up.<br /> <br /> Bake a cake. feed half to sick and half to volunteer/victim. Now the status effects are swapped.<br /> <br /> Guy got a stab infection, find the knife, boil it, feed stab victim the broth. Now hes better.<br /> <br /> Scare a chicken, now it lays eggs that hatch into vipers (easy antivenom source). Thaumatergy is weird dude.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:46:05-08:00","id":817028,"title":"","content":"I feel like Thaumaurgy should feel like a miracle, even if it's just a minor miracle. It shouldn't require magical objects or outside sources of essence, it should just be... Heh, this one weird trick you can do.<br /> <br /> For inspiration, I'd go back to superstitions and miracles that people have claimed through history. Maybe this mother knows the right prayer to say so that her kiss actually can banish pain or ward off infection and maybe this person knows the right sequence of knocks to get a bit of luck from knocking on wood. <br /> <br /> Don't focus too much on the effect, because it's invariably going to be either a narrative thing or a minor bonus, like a +1 to your next disease resistance roll. Focus on how the ritual works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T18:03:54-08:00","id":817286,"title":"","content":"Honestly?<br /> <br /> I've just been taking Thaumaturgical rituals from 2nd ed and porting them over. Not the rolls and stuff, but the effects and their general power level.<br /> <br /> There's a shaman in the Elk tribe who knows the song to sing to call an elk from the forest to lay its head in your lap and sleep while the hunters creep up with their spears. Old Art of Husbandry.<br /> <br /> There's an exorcist in Sijan who knows the trick of using the blood of the living mixed with salt to ward an area against the unquiet dead. Old Art of Warding.<br /> <br /> There's a sorcerer's apprentice who has been blessed by dark powers with the ability to fuel his rituals through bloodletting and ritual sacrifice-old Art of the Dead, spending HLs for motes.<br /> <br /> There's a doctor in Nexus who knows how to concoct liquids that react and change colors when exposed to various substances. The Guild pays him handsomely when he consults on criminal investigations of losses they've incurred. Old art of alchemy.<br /> <br /> There's a little peasant kid in the Realm who can find his way unerringly through the manses of the Dragonblooded and the ruins of the First Age to the chamber where the hearthstone forms, purely by instinct. They keep sending him into First Age ruins full of dangerous traps and he keeps coming out alive...for now. Old school art of Geomancy.<br /> <br /> Just give people one or two neat tricks each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T18:15:20-08:00","id":817295,"title":"","content":"Did I miss something or could anybody with Occult do Sorcerous Workings these days? I could not find any requirement that you actually have to be initialized into the appropriate circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T18:35:00-08:00","id":817309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817295#post817295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I miss something or could anybody with Occult do Sorcerous Workings these days? I could not find any requirement that you actually have to be initialized into the appropriate circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a &quot;sorcerer&quot; is both a distinct in setting/character trait and a rules mechanic one. On the &quot;Spells and Sorcerous Workings&quot; section, pages 464-465 it is said:<br /> <br /> &quot;Workings require considerable time and effort to complete, and their expansive scope often requires the Storyteller and the <b>sorcerer\u2019s player</b> to work together in defining its precise effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that establishes that to execute sorcerous workings you must be a sorcerer. It then lets you how to do that when playing a Solar on page 465 and how to become a sorcerer if playing a mortal on the sidebar on page 470.<br /> <br /> The intent seems pretty clear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T19:38:04-08:00","id":817340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817286#post817286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<br /> <br /> I've just been taking Thaumaturgical rituals from 2nd ed and porting them over. Not the rolls and stuff, but the effects and their general power level. <br /> <br /> Just give people one or two neat tricks each.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great idea and I am totally going to do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T20:04:17-08:00","id":817354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817340#post817340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great idea and I am totally going to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also handy when the player of a Sorcerer wants to know what the gets out of his Thaumaturgy toys. I'll have the PC pick a handful of rituals he knows, and say he can learn more if he meets miracle workers who know them.<br /> <br /> Solar Sorcerer Ostentatious Ritual might know a couple spells...and also know how to whistle the note that puts bees to sleep so you can harvest their honey, and know the way to dance to perform to cause embers to roar into a campfire that dances along with you even if it's raining, and know how to weave straw into a rope that can bind a ghost so it can't leave a corpse to wander at night...but he doesn't know how to take a man's hair and weave it into a knot that spells out his name and burn it at sunset to call the man on the wind and compel him to walk to you across hundreds of miles!<br /> <br /> But when a rival sorceress uses that ritual on him, if he answers her summons instead of resisting...he might have a chance to steal knowledge of that miracle from her, if he's clever.<br /> <br /> (Arts of Husbandry, Alchemy, The Dead, and Husbandry again, in 2E terms)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:35:09-08:00","id":817421,"title":"","content":"Eh... 3E thaumaturgy really didn't wow me. Maybe it's cause they couldn't really fit enough example in or something? I rather miss the formulaic schools of thaumaturgy from 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:55:06-08:00","id":817463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817286#post817286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<br /> <br /> I've just been taking Thaumaturgical rituals from 2nd ed and porting them over. Not the rolls and stuff, but the effects and their general power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a reasonable idea, try to keep in mind that Thaumaturgy should be reserved for things that are genuinely miraculous, not mere applications of skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a shaman in the Elk tribe who knows the song to sing to call an elk from the forest to lay its head in your lap and sleep while the hunters creep up with their spears. Old Art of Husbandry. </div> </div> </div>This could be thaumaturgy, but it could also be Performance or Survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's an exorcist in Sijan who knows the trick of using the blood of the living mixed with salt to ward an area against the unquiet dead. Old Art of Warding. </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely a mundane Occult roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a sorcerer's apprentice who has been blessed by dark powers with the ability to fuel his rituals through bloodletting and ritual sacrifice-old Art of the Dead, spending HLs for motes. </div> </div> </div>You hardly need thaumaturgy to use sacrifices in sorcerous rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a doctor in Nexus who knows how to concoct liquids that react and change colors when exposed to various substances. The Guild pays him handsomely when he consults on criminal investigations of losses they've incurred. Old art of alchemy. </div> </div> </div>Mundane Craft(Alchemy)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a little peasant kid in the Realm who can find his way unerringly through the manses of the Dragonblooded and the ruins of the First Age to the chamber where the hearthstone forms, purely by instinct. They keep sending him into First Age ruins full of dangerous traps and he keeps coming out alive...for now. Old school art of Geomancy. </div> </div> </div>Sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T05:26:47-08:00","id":817535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817421#post817421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... 3E thaumaturgy really didn't wow me. Maybe it's cause they couldn't really fit enough example in or something? I rather miss the formulaic schools of thaumaturgy from 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them were maybe ok. Others were really stupid (needing Occult to breed mundane animals pretty well, anyone?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:05:07-08:00","id":817604,"title":"","content":"Anyone know a list of 2e books that listed Thaumaturgy rituals? I have most of the books but it's been years since I've read that and I always glossed Thaumaturgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:26:33-08:00","id":817629,"title":"","content":"The trouble is that what the book calls &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; in 3E doesn't really feel like what it has been presented as in the past. Most of what we, as legacy players of Exalted, think of as Thaumaturgy is now just applications of Occult, Medicine, and Lore in a mundane sense - and that can be a good thing. You know the rituals to do things &quot;mundanely,&quot; and it looks like magic because magic is just a part of Creation. Salt to ward off ghosts, iron to ward off the Fae, a treatment of burning incense and prayer to drive off disease spirits, a harvest dance to increase its abundance and a fertility festival to enrich the planting, all magical things, all rituals that are &quot;thaumaturgy&quot; in the old sense, but are just part of how things work in Creation and thus mundane applications of Abilities.<br /> <br /> What 3E calls &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; are really random 1-2 point supernatural merits that amount to unique minor tricks some random people can perform. This one guy who can break bread into more food than the original loaf, and this other who can smell spirits, and this girl who can listen to a sea shell to hear her twin brother's voice while he's at sea are all 3E thaumaturges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:36:26-08:00","id":817641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817629#post817629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trouble is that what the book calls &amp;quot;Thaumaturgy&amp;quot; in 3E doesn't really feel like what it has been presented as in the past. Most of what we, as legacy players of Exalted, think of as Thaumaturgy is now just applications of Occult, Medicine, and Lore in a mundane sense - and that can be a good thing. You know the rituals to do things &amp;quot;mundanely,&amp;quot; and it looks like magic because magic is just a part of Creation. Salt to ward off ghosts, iron to ward off the Fae, a treatment of burning incense and prayer to drive off disease spirits, a harvest dance to increase its abundance and a fertility festival to enrich the planting, all magical things, all rituals that are &amp;quot;thaumaturgy&amp;quot; in the old sense, but are just part of how things work in Creation and thus mundane applications of Abilities.<br /> <br /> What 3E calls &amp;quot;Thaumaturgy&amp;quot; are really random 1-2 point supernatural merits that amount to unique minor tricks some random people can perform. This one guy who can break bread into more food than the original loaf, and this other who can smell spirits, and this girl who can listen to a sea shell to hear her twin brother's voice while he's at sea are all 3E thaumaturges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea it looks like glorified mutations for now. Im going to wait for the magic book? If thats a thing? Maybe theyll elaborate on it. For now it looks like its just thier to keep the term for brand recognition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:49:53-08:00","id":817654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817604#post817604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know a list of 2e books that listed Thaumaturgy rituals? I have most of the books but it's been years since I've read that and I always glossed Thaumaturgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the majority are in the core and the Codex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:53:39-08:00","id":817655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817641#post817641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea it looks like glorified mutations for now. Im going to wait for the magic book? If thats a thing? Maybe theyll elaborate on it. For now it looks like its just thier to keep the term for brand recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's Paths of Brigid, yeah. I'm stoked for that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:00:29-08:00","id":818060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817535#post817535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of them were maybe ok. Others were really stupid (needing Occult to breed mundane animals pretty well, anyone?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall, weren't <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">some of the Procedures learnable with no occult dots?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:59:01-08:00","id":818759,"title":"","content":"After reading this thread, I realize that many of the Ex2 Thaumaturgy rituals now fall under the Occult ability. For example, my Occult 5 Twilight no longer needs to buy a ritual to be able to place a ward on someone's house. To me this is a good change.<br /> <br /> The next question is does a non-Exalt need to buy the Thaumaturgy Merit to cast wards and so on? Or does that merit just give a mortal access to &quot;Miracles&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, something occurred to me: Exalts can pump Essence into actions to make the action more likely to succeed. So while a Thaumaturgy ritual that imitates an an Occult/Medicine action may be useless to an Exalt, it would be extremely beneficial to a mortal. The ritual would be worth it to a mortal if increases the likelihood of the action succeeding.<br /> <br /> For example, Lin's patient has a life-threatening fever. If Lin was a Solar, she could use her supernatural excellence at healing to bring the fever down. However, Lin is a mortal, so channeling Essence for a better chance of success isn't an option for her. Since Lin is a Thaumaturgist, she knows a ritual to break a fever, so she is able to save her patient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:15:35-08:00","id":818821,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I feel like thaumaturgists are meant to be little miracles. &quot;Tricks&quot;, sure, but they're not reproduceable by almost anyone else, and are done in ways that feel strange and occult. The value of them on a sorcerer is that they let you have magic that is less dramatic than butterflies that feels like <i>magic</i>. They're great for a few specific scenarios, they're great for worldbuilding. Give an NPC hermit a couple really strange habits that lead to unique powers! And make them <i>weird</i> but useful... like... the wanderer on the road who will tell your future for some coin. The hermit in the hills who can brew a tea which will bring clarity to a memory so strong that you feel you're reliving it. The witch in the bog who forms an effigy of you with some hair and a vial of blood mixed into clay, who says it will break if you suffer any harm, no matter how far away... the idea is just that they help a character feel more... well, magical. Even if they don't know the big dramatic miracle of<i> sorcery</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Stuff I've made:<br /> Ex3 Combat Flowchart &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07uuoct/Exalted%203rd%20Combat.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07...d%20Combat.png</a><br /> Ex3 Battlegroup Cheatsheet &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe4kzhq/Exalted%203e%20Battlegroups.png?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe...roups.png?dl=0</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9361-givenflesh","name":"GivenFlesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9361_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:37:59-08:00","id":819425,"title":"","content":"My reading is that thaumaturgy is there for a blanket 'I know how do to something that is not normal in the setting, kinda breaks the rules, and I don't want to give to other players, is not reproducable, but is awesome.' <br /> <br /> If it is something that lots of people know, it should be covered by regular skills. If it is calling on a god or spirit, it should be covered by regular skills.<br /> <br /> If you can't explain it, and no one else can do it, it's thaumaturgy. Here's some of my ideas.<br /> <br /> Speak to badgers. You speak any regular language, they understand. You understand their snuffles and squeaks. They are reasonably friendly (they are still badgers, though, so watch yourself).<br /> <br /> Ask a question, reference a book, and get something resembling an answer. <br /> <br /> Pull the ribs out of a pig fully cooked without harming the pig. Not marinated and no sauce.<br /> <br /> Always be able to find sometuing that has been mundanely and legitimately lost. Not stolen, not deliberately hidden, but lost. Lost sheep? Lost tools? Lost city?<br /> <br /> Touch an object and be able to see from it while touching it. Touch a tree to survey the land from the top of a tree. Touch a wall to see the other side.<br /> <br /> Do something other people can do, but without the difficulty. Write on paper by speaking to it. <br /> <br /> My rules: no dice tricks. It doesn't work if specifically blocked by other magic. It doesn't work of another person tried the same thing. The magic resides in you, not in an object made or procedure used. If you make a cake that helps to heal, it only works if you serve it. You can't industrualize it. If you need to make a pie, the magic stops when you make another pie. Generally make it something really impossible, but not big.<br /> <br /> Edited for typos because my thumbs are fat and my phone small.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2132,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","user":"Ejtaka","date":". 01-29-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:53:23-08:00","id":819485,"title":"","content":"That does seem to be what it is. I just wish they hadn't called it &quot;thaumaturgy,&quot; because it fits neither the old editions' definition nor mythic/historical definitions. They're random supernatural tricks better represented by mutation/merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:55:19-08:00","id":819487,"title":"","content":"I guess I need to start using the term &quot;Occultist&quot; for mortals who dabble in magic instead of &quot;Thaumaturge&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T18:21:23-08:00","id":819622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=819425#post819425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pull the ribs out of a pig fully cooked without harming the pig. <b>Not marinated and no sauce.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>what kind of diabolical villain are you<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T20:21:32-08:00","id":819659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=819425#post819425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My reading is that thaumaturgy is there for a blanket 'I know how do to something that is not normal in the setting, kinda breaks the rules, and <b>I don't want to give to other players, is not reproducable, but is awesome</b>.'<br /> <br /> If you can't explain it, and <b>no one else can do it</b>, it's thaumaturgy. Here's some of my ideas....</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that thaumaturgy is something someone can learn from a person capable doing specific tricks if they will teach you and you have the capacity to learn thaumaturgy (by having the merit as a mortal, or just being an exalt with terrestrial sorcery.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:47:00-08:00","id":819925,"title":"","content":"Let me rephrase. Something you don't want every pc picking up because it is that useful, and something you don't want the pcs teaching every villager and farmer. What I don't want is super scifi games because the pcs teach super science courses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T15:08:39-08:00","id":820001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817629#post817629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trouble is that what the book calls &quot;Thaumaturgy&quot; in 3E doesn't really feel like what it has been presented as in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=819485#post819485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does seem to be what it is. I just wish they hadn't called it &quot;thaumaturgy,&quot; because it fits neither the old editions' definition nor mythic/historical definitions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's solidly on you, and not the job of the book, to dispose of notions you've carried forward from the past editions.<br /> <br /> I get that that can be frustrating and difficult, but, it is what it is, and the writers have basically been saying this for months if not years before the backer release to try and get people prepared for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817629#post817629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of what we, as legacy players of Exalted, think of as Thaumaturgy is now just applications of Occult, Medicine, and Lore in a mundane sense - and that can be a good thing. You know the rituals to do things &quot;mundanely,&quot; and it looks like magic because magic is just a part of Creation. Salt to ward off ghosts, iron to ward off the Fae, a treatment of burning incense and prayer to drive off disease spirits, a harvest dance to increase its abundance and a fertility festival to enrich the planting, all magical things, all rituals that are &quot;thaumaturgy&quot; in the old sense, but are just part of how things work in Creation and thus mundane applications of Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually love it. It makes more sense to me to gate those things behind &quot;stuff you can basically learn&quot; but not take it to the level of pseudo-scientific applications. Warding and the like feels very much like hedge magic, but something rooted in folk knowledge and tradition, but actually being &quot;mundane&quot; in nature (or rather, mundane in the world of Creation - these are not <i>supernatural</i> effects in-setting, they're wholly <i>natural</i> effects, given the way Creation works - magic and spirits are proven to exist, prayers have actual and provable impact in-setting upon spirits, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:29:54-08:00","id":820900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=820001#post820001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's solidly on you, and not the job of the book, to dispose of notions you've carried forward from the past editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if Ex3 had said that Charms were not the powers of the Exalted, but were instead things in which anybody can develop power by following certain 5-dot progressions, that wouldn't be a poor design decision, because it's the responsibility of the player to adapt to whatever the new edition calls for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=820001#post820001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that that can be frustrating and difficult, but, it is what it is, and the writers have basically been saying this for months if not years before the backer release to try and get people prepared for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't change that it was a bad choice. &quot;Hey, guys, Ford Motors speaking, here; we're going to be rolling out our 2020 line of trucks as 1-door vehicles with no bed, a 200-lb frame, and just a single seat for a driver with storage in the form of gift cards to U-Haul to rent trailers! Just a heads up, so you're aware.&quot; Yeah, doesn't make the decision any better just because we have 4 years to &quot;prepare&quot; for it.<br /> <br /> Snark aside, if what they rolled out as &quot;thaumaturgy&quot; was not better, more cleanly, and with less word-count represented by a merit called, say, &quot;minor miracle (o-ooo)&quot; and thus wouldn't require the multi-page dedication to trying to justify calling it something that has a lot of baggage in Exalted, I wouldn't be complaining.<br /> <br /> Heck, &quot;Occult is used to perform thaumaturgy, the folk magic and science of creation that includes[list of things, and common difficulties]. Like melee or lore, knowledge of the occult is all that's required to make the attempt,&quot; would have gotten barely a blip of complaint, would have held to both real-world arguable definitions of the word and to expectations from prior editions, and not even been a change from the rules we've been presented, since what most people are looking for in thaumaturgy HAS been rolled into a generic use of Occult. Which is good.<br /> <br /> It's just a really, really weird choice of insisting that thaumaturgy is something entirely different and unique but not really worth players' attention, in multiple pages of text, while not pointing back to the Occult skill to help those looking for what it used to be. This choice causes friction and problems where there needn't have been. And thus, I wish they'd chosen differently.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=820001#post820001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually love it. It makes more sense to me to gate those things behind &quot;stuff you can basically learn&quot; but not take it to the level of pseudo-scientific applications. Warding and the like feels very much like hedge magic, but something rooted in folk knowledge and tradition, but actually being &quot;mundane&quot; in nature (or rather, mundane in the world of Creation - these are not <i>supernatural</i> effects in-setting, they're wholly <i>natural</i> effects, given the way Creation works - magic and spirits are proven to exist, prayers have actual and provable impact in-setting upon spirits, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! Glad you like it. I don't mind the mechanics. I just think the name is a bad choice, and a huge waste of word-count to justify it while muddying the issue and diminishing clarity for those coming from earlier editions and looking for something specific (i.e. that which is now just something you can do by rolling Occult).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T06:38:03-08:00","id":820929,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Thaumaturgy literally mean &quot;miracle working&quot;? How is the current system not <i>more</i> fitting for this name than the magical natural science of yore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T06:38:29-08:00","id":820930,"title":"","content":"I suggest stealing stuff from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unknown_Armies\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Unknown Armies</i></a>. Ritual magick and some Adept powers from that game fall into the same category as what 3E calls &quot;thaumaturgy.&quot;<br /> <br /> * Stay awake for more than 48 hours. The hallucinations you experience from that point on give you precognitive or postcognitive insight into the events around you.<br /> <br /> * Make some kind of gamble that could get you hurt (e.g. &quot;I'll flip a coin. Heads, I'll slam this door on your fingers. Tails, you slam this door on my fingers.&quot;), and do not cheat. Surrendering to fate now gives you the ability to manipulate probability in your favor later on.<br /> <br /> * Keep a little jar of someone's blood, hair, and urine mixed together. Looking at the color of the liquid will tell you if that person is currently healthy, injured, or dead.<br /> <br /> * Make a really good mask of a person. For a short time while you wear it, you are able to <i>think</i> as that person, maybe even becoming privy to knowledge that only they have.<br /> <br /> * When you are drunk enough to have your judgement seriously impaired, you are also uncannily tough.<br /> <br /> * By periodically cutting yourself, you gain a limited ability to reshape your own flesh.<br /> <br /> * Actual, functional voodoo dolls.<br /> <br /> * Actual, functional love potions (maybe more like obsession potions, depending).<br /> <br /> * Instill autonomy into a special doll you made by sacrificing emotionally important memories. The more important the memory, the more sapient the doll will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-01-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:02:37-08:00","id":820988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=820929#post820929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't Thaumaturgy literally mean &amp;quot;miracle working&amp;quot;? How is the current system not <i>more</i> fitting for this name than the magical natural science of yore?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thaumaturgy\" target=\"_blank\">While it has been used in a way appropriate to the current usage, the older use for the term does have a noticeable real-world precedent. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:07:22-08:00","id":820991,"title":"","content":"I would also contend that, while the term &quot;minor miracle&quot; is used in the Ex3 book to describe them, they are such underwhelming (albeit unique) magical effects compared to some of the mundane magic that Occult can do, let alone the Charms of Spirits or the Exalted, that terming them &quot;miracles&quot; is stretching the definition of the term considerably. &quot;He can detach and re-attach his thumb, but only with his other hand and only while sliding it along in a 'ritual' fashion!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:28:07-08:00","id":821294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=820991#post820991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also contend that, while the term &quot;minor miracle&quot; is used in the Ex3 book to describe them, they are such underwhelming (albeit unique) magical effects compared to some of the mundane magic that Occult can do, let alone the Charms of Spirits or the Exalted, that terming them &quot;miracles&quot; is stretching the definition of the term considerably. &quot;He can detach and re-attach his thumb, but only with his other hand and only while sliding it along in a 'ritual' fashion!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> Reading Tea Leaves - you can see the future, an ability of oracles and prophets that held sway over entire nations, nay, cultures!<br /> <br /> Unquenchable Flame - What manner of man are you that can summon up fire without flint or tinder?<br /> <br /> Second Bread - Admittedly nerfed compared to the source material, but it emulates a miracle Jesus himself performed! Also, in olden times, loaves of bread could get quite big, so it can potentially create more than what passes for a loaf nowadays.<br /> <br /> Exorcism - an ability possessed, among others, by Jesus and his chosen Apostles. In a world rife with evil spirits, being able to cast one out without bargaining is no mean feat.<br /> <br /> Speak With Ozashun - commune with... whatever Ozashun is, but generally a unique being with supernatural knowledge of what happens throughout his area of influence.<br /> <br /> Knowing either Reading Tea Leaves, Speak With Ozashun or Exorcism will not only win you bread for the rest of your life, it will make you an important figure in whatever society you're in - in the first two cases, even the Exalted may need your unique gifts (less so with Exorcism, but then again, not every Exalt comes loaded with ways of dealing with unruly spirits).<br /> <br /> Of the remaining two (which are notably one-dot rituals, i.e. truly lesser miracles), Unquenchable Flame is easily impressive enough for the wilderness-dwellers to make you a legend among your people - less useful in the civilized areas, but something tells me you're not supposed to be born with this gift in the City of Thousand Braziers and Free Torch Refills Every Saturnday.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Second Bread may have been written solely as a setup for a joke about Jesus getting beat up in Nexus, but even then, the duplication of matter is clearly miraculous.<br /> <br /> In summary, nope, not being underwhelmed in the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T05:35:11-08:00","id":821563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're less impressive than things that can be done by a wider range of things. &quot;Wow! You can score a basket from 10 feet away without distractions 1 in 3 times! And you're the only man alive with exactly that skill level! ...but most college and pro basketball players can do it from a free-throw line 1:2 times.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Tea Leaves - you can see the future, an ability of oracles and prophets that held sway over entire nations, nay, cultures!</div> </div> </div> </div>And, if they hadn't called it out explicitly as an example of this, it would fall right in there with the Occult rolls to know how to ward off fae and ghosts, to propitiate spirits and gods, or to divine the best time to set sail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unquenchable Flame - What manner of man are you that can summon up fire without flint or tinder?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only mortal in the world who can do this! But far better-known are the Fire Aspect Dragonblooded, who can...do much more than that. And are less rare. This just isn't that impressive, and a Survival roll of sufficient successes can let somebody do something functionally similar (if only because they can MacGuyver up faux flint). It's cute, but it's not a &quot;miracle.&quot; Not compared to what others can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Bread - Admittedly nerfed compared to the source material, but it emulates a miracle Jesus himself performed! Also, in olden times, loaves of bread could get quite big, so it can potentially create more than what passes for a loaf nowadays.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a miracle because there weren't comparable things being done. Jesus's actions are, aside from the whole Atonement and Resurrection thing, barely Herculean. What made Him stand out in then-current myth was how very differently He acted than common legends about supernatural heroes, and the fact that He was the only one around at the time. What makes Him stand out now is that Christians believe He really existed and did these things. (And, again, when you put the Atonement back in, it is awe-inspiring, beyond anything even the Exalted can do.)<br /> <br /> But the bread-and-fishes miracle was miraculous in scale and in comparison to the lack of other things other beings can do. It's comparable in effect and awesomeness to manna from heaven, which even mortal sorcerers can do. And again, there's ONE guy who can do the &quot;double a loaf&quot; trick, and hundreds of sorcerers (at minimum) who can call down bread from heaven sufficient to feed a village.<br /> <br /> It's noteworthy, but not a &quot;miracle&quot; compared to what a more common and famous subset of beings can do in-setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exorcism - an ability possessed, among others, by Jesus and his chosen Apostles. In a world rife with evil spirits, being able to cast one out without bargaining is no mean feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And REALLY should be something Occult can do; yes, Christ did it, as did His apostles. And a number of priests throughout history in any number of religions (at least reputedly; obviously, whether you accept other faiths and even Christ and His followers' actions as true is a matter of faith).<br /> <br /> Shinto priests and mikos, Buddhist monks, Hindu ritualists, faith healers and Catholic exorcists have all done this kind of thing. It's not a unique thing to Christ and His followers, at least by reputation. Nor should it be &quot;just one guy in a generation, throughout all Creation.&quot; And it isn't, since at least Solars and probably other Exalted (even Dynasts) can pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speak With Ozashun - commune with... whatever Ozashun is, but generally a unique being with supernatural knowledge of what happens throughout his area of influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And any sorcerer can invent a spell to contact some otherworldly knowledgeable being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing either Reading Tea Leaves, Speak With Ozashun or Exorcism will not only win you bread for the rest of your life, it will make you an important figure in whatever society you're in - in the first two cases, even the Exalted may need your unique gifts (less so with Exorcism, but then again, not every Exalt comes loaded with ways of dealing with unruly spirits).</div> </div> </div> </div>It can, but only if the ST decides randomly that no other fortune telling exists (which makes little sense, as it's hardly a thing on the list of &quot;just doesn't happen in Exalted&quot; and is a pretty standard staple trope of the genres Exalted emulates). &quot;Uh, this is a miracle because we've arbitrarily taken it from commonplace to rare. Never mind that Sidereals do it better. I hope nobody ever writes a Sorcery spell that does divination, or this will look silly again! What do you mean you think it should be an Occult roll anybody can do? Of course not, because, um... it's special! Yeah!&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821294#post821294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In summary, nope, not being underwhelmed in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm only impressed if you remove the Exalted - including the Terrestrials - and sorcerers from the setting. Otherwise, this is at best &quot;oh, so you're a weak sorcerer&quot; level of reaction. Sure, impressive if you're the one magic-guy this group of mortals have met, but when your super-rare &quot;miracle&quot; is less impressive than comparable, less-rare effects...<br /> <br /> It reminds me of a problem I had with Melanie Rawn's Sunrunners. Sunrunners could do neat stuff &quot;weaving light&quot; with the bright light of the sun, and sometimes even off of campfires and torches. Sorcerers could do that, AND pull it from even the faint light of the stars. Sorcerers also had more powers. There really wasn't anything I could ever remember seeing Sunrunners do that Sorcerers couldn't, and lots that Sorcerers could that Sunrunners couldn't. But the rarity of Sunrunners was played up compared to the relative commonality of Sorcerers, and having both bloodlines was supposed to be really impressive. I never got it: why care if somebody is both a Sunrunner and a Sorcerer? He can't do anything more or better than a Sorcerer who is not also a Sunrunner. Sunrunners being rarer didn't make them better.<br /> <br /> In a world where 85% of people are right-handed, 14% are ambidexterous, and 1% are left-handed, being left-handed isn't more impressive just because it's rarer than ambidexterity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T05:42:23-08:00","id":821571,"title":"","content":"More ideas:<br /> <br /> * Melt down the weapons of warriors you have killed. Turn them into rings, bracelets, or other jewelry. Wearing their bling will grant you a measure of your fallen enemies' strength.<br /> * If someone you know gets stabbed, find the weapon and bathe it in rosewater. Sing to it, polish it, and rest it on a cushion somewhere warm. The injury will be miraculously healed, but if the pampered weapon gets removed from its place of comfort, then the wound will return at once.<br /> * You know the secret language of a particular kind of animal - cats, horses, dogs, and rats are the most common.<br /> * You always know which way is North, even if you are underground.<br /> * You can make people forget talking to you or seeing you, although this gets more difficult if you talk to them a lot or they see you often.<br /> * You never get sick. Ever.<br /> * You can turn lead into gold or iron into silver with a special chemical mixture that other people cannot reproduce.<br /> * You can break small and/or fragile objects by focusing on them for a minute.<br /> * You can mend small and uncomplicated objects by focusing on them for a minute.<br /> * You can change the colors of fabric by spitting on them.<br /> * You can sometimes pull birds or small mammals out of your hat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821563#post821563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a world where 85% of people are right-handed, 14% are ambidexterous, and 1% are left-handed, being left-handed isn't more impressive just because it's rarer than ambidexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument appears to be entirely predicated on the assumption that thaumaturgy - ALL thaumaturgy, not just one specific gift - is rarer than either sorcery or exaltation. Why do you assume that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-02-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T05:58:14-08:00","id":821576,"title":"","content":"And where, pray tell, did you get the idea that either sorcery or being an Exalt of any kind is more common in the setting than Thaumaturgy is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:46:30-08:00","id":821611,"title":"","content":"I've been rereading the Thaumaturgy Merit and what is the benefit of it outside getting access to the rituals? What is the advantage of an Exalted Sorcerer having Thaumaturgy in addition to Sorcery? Is there a point to buying Thaumaturgy if you don't buy any of the rituals? Does a character get a connection to the Essence of Creation? Sort of an Unseen Sense? Does using a line of salt for ward work better for a Thaumaturgst than a mortal without the merit?<br /> <br /> Edited to add: I think this may be a difference in RPG theory views. Exalted has always had &quot;Gatekeeper XP Costs&quot; - You have to buy Terrestrial Sorcery to have the ability to buy other charms. It's one of the things that was house ruled away in our Skype game (When you buy Terrestrial Sorcery, you get Emerald Counterspell too.)<br /> <br /> I'll probably do something similar with Thaumaturgy. Give the character with the merit the ability to roll Perception + Occult to sense the Essence Flow of an area or something. Exalts can refine that ability with charms to get detailed information about the Essence of an area or see dematerialized beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-02-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:47:03-08:00","id":821612,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth noting that The Shadow Puppeteers of An-Teng are still around and are mentioned by name in the corebook and they've historically always been Thaumaturges (&quot;Mortal Sorcerers&quot; when that was the appropriate term back when Blood and Salt was published).<br /> <br /> So whatever the overall numbers are in Creation, there's probably enough in An-Teng's Shorelands to ruin your day with shadowy murder spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-02-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:49:18-08:00","id":821616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821576#post821576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where, pray tell, did you get the idea that either sorcery or being an Exalt of any kind is more common in the setting than Thaumaturgy is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 490: &quot;Mortal thaumaturges are exceedingly rare.&quot; It doesn't say it is rarer than Exaltation of any type, but I can see where someone could draw that conclusion. Personally, I believe there are enough Thaumaturges around to make a recruiting them for certain positions (Sijan Funeralists, Seventh Legion Sorcerer Engineers, etc) viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:04:24-08:00","id":821624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821616#post821616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">viable</div> </div> </div> </div>There's that word again. We really need to add that to the <a href=\"http://shatterwing.com/buzzwords.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">buzzwords</a>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Fuck flood detection!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:07:52-08:00","id":821626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821624#post821624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's that word again. We really need to add that to the <a href=\"http://shatterwing.com/buzzwords.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">buzzwords</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did Viable become a naughty word? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:13:47-08:00","id":821630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821626#post821626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did Viable become a naughty word? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't say it was <i>naughty</i>. Just that it's become one of those meaningless buzzwords on this forum. <br /> <br /> Actually, John M\u00f8rke said it better anyway, so I'll just quote him...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/371628-i-just-realized-due-to-sorcerous-workings-sorcery-is-likely-to-get-a-lot-blastier?p=373436#post373436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly &quot;combat viable.&quot; This word entails a value judgment, and I have seen it used multiple times in this thread, and each person seems to have a different idea of what makes something viable, which leads to a slurry of posts that do not follow one to the next and a conversation that goes nowhere. Recognize first that there is no standard definition for combat viability. Unless you explain your standard for viability, your point is incoherent.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/371628-i-just-realized-due-to-sorcerous-workings-sorcery-is-likely-to-get-a-lot-blastier?p=374073#post374073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably have said something like [sorcery is viable in combat in 3E] in the past, yes, and I stand by it with the caveat that my above post about viability has always applied. What I consider viable is not always what the customer thinks is viable, and I long ago learned that when some people say viable, what they really mean is optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:21:20-08:00","id":821635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821630#post821630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't say it was <i>naughty</i>. Just that it's become one of those meaningless buzzwords on this forum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can I use feasible instead? Realistic? <br /> <br /> Basically, what I am trying to say is this:<br /> <br /> Many locations have positions (Sijan Funeralists, Seventh Legion Sorcerer Engineers, etc) for Thamaugurists which need to be filled. I am assuming there are enough Thamaugurists around for those positions to actually be filled. <br /> <br /> (Sorry, might be a bit sensitive about word choice. I'm trying to remove meaningless words from my writing. ) <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:39:20-08:00","id":821642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821635#post821635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use feasible instead? Realistic?<br /> <br /> Basically, what I am trying to say is this:<br /> <br /> [snip]<br /> <br /> (Sorry, might be a bit sensitive about word choice. I'm trying to remove meaningless words from my writing. )</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you were saying, man, I was just poking fun at how often I see the word flung around here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Sorry if I made ya feel bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:53:31-08:00","id":821654,"title":"","content":"I hope I'm not the only one interested in actually devising thaumaturgical gifts, here. <br /> <br /> * Your singing of certain hymns repels demons. <br /> * You can summon the ghosts of people who are recently departed, allowing them to possess your body for a short time while another person talks to them. <br /> * You really can make plants healthier by talking to them. <br /> * You can trap some kinds of Fair Folk in a room by drawing an erratic pattern of lines through it in chalk or charcoal - for some reason, they feel compelled not to cross any of the lines. <br /> * Drinking your special ginseng tea twice a day for a week will cure most mundane diseases. <br /> * You can push small quantities of water around with a gesture. You won't part the Red Sea, but with a little work you can cross a creek without getting your feet wet. <br /> * You can make actual, functional dreamcatchers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:06:46-08:00","id":821703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821654#post821654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope I'm not the only one interested in actually devising thaumaturgical gifts, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not! You're just better at it than some of us. Me, not least among them. Keep em comin!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:32:48-08:00","id":821755,"title":"","content":"Not a backer, so these might not work.<br /> <br /> \u2022Nonmagical animals won't attack you unless you attack them first.<br /> <br /> \u2022You smell ozone whenever someone spends Essence. You don't know who or what or why, just that it happened.<br /> <br /> \u2022Your tears heal blindness.<br /> <br /> \u2022Any land you tend is slightly more fertile than it should be.<br /> <br /> \u2022When you bleed on metal while you're forging it, it becomes stronger than normal.<br /> <br /> \u2022You can turn rocks into cheese. Just cheese. Hopefully, you are not lactose intolerant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:45:48-08:00","id":821770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821703#post821703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not! You're just better at it than some of us. Me, not least among them. Keep em comin!</div> </div> </div> </div>As you wish (I am bored today).<br /> <br /> Folk superstitions and rituals are another good source of thaumaturgy too. Like the tea leaf-reading, many people might believe they have these abilities (or convince others that they have them), but only rarely are their powers genuine.<br /> <br /> * You have a twin sister or brother with whom you sometimes share thoughts. With some concentration, you can telepathically communicate even over great distances. <br /> * You can see through magical illusions using some kind of special tool - a mirror, a stone with a hole bored through it, or perhaps an heirloom telescope. <br /> * You may summon rain with dances, invocations, and the construction of strange tower-like structures.<br /> * You can eat inedible things. They do not provide you any nourishment, but you can eat them just the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T13:32:35-08:00","id":821847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821635#post821635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use feasible instead? Realistic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use viable. Use it fiercely and excessively, such that it is branded into the skull of your enemy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here are those rituals I promised you.<br /> <br /> <b>Eiderdown Death (\u2022)</b><br /> At sunset, the thaumaturge anoints the sick and dying with sunflower oil (or that of any local staple crop). This ensures that he will sleep peacefully until dawn, no matter what pain wracks his body. Should he die before the sun's fully risen, his lower soul accepts the way of things, and bothers no one unless they touch the corpse.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisp-Catching Shell (\u2022)</b><br /> The thaumaturge has knowledge of a certain symbol, the pronunciation of which is lost to the ages. By scribing it on some small container (such as a seashell or a cricket cage), she may use it to catch someone's dying breath. Once caught, that mote of dying Essence can be used in the treatment of the same condition that caused it; this reduces any penalties to a Medicine roll by 3.<br /> <br /> A gathered breath only lasts for a few days unless stored in a hermetic container, but can be used as a component for antidotes or medicine with a longer shelf life.<br /> <br /> <b>Raiton's Delight (\u2022)</b><br /> By leaning close to a corpse and meeting its gaze, a thaumaturge may see what made it. Deep in the dark of its eyes, there is an impression of the last significant thing it saw in life, preserved until the skull is empty.<br /> A blind thaumaturge may still use Raiton's Delight, but must sniff or lick the corpse's eyeballs to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Beckon the Yellow Prince (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Through a hour-long ritual dance, a thaumaturge can turn the victim of an illness into a conduit for divinity. At the end of the dance, roll (Charisma + Occult) against the Morbidity of the illness. On a success, a little god of that disease is contacted, and may speak and be spoken to through the sufferer's mouth and wounds. On a failure, the same thing happens, except that the spirit is offended by the disturbance, ill-tempered by nature, or just an idiot.<br /> <br /> <b>Laugh in Saturn's Face (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Under the noonday sun, the thaumaturge cuts out the heart of another (or her own, if she can bear the pain). Whispering sweet nothings to the heart, she keeps it pumping and its owner alive, just long enough for a live songbird to be sealed inside his chest. Then the heart dies, while the subject lives on for ever and ever, or at least until the songbird slips free.<br /> <br /> A subject of Laugh in Saturn's Face can heal lethal damage to his Incapacitated health level, and never dies from sickness, deprivation, or age (though he still grows old). If the songbird is released, he wastes away over the course of three days, his soul denied reincarnation and afterlife.<br /> <br /> (Though, now that I look at them, I'm not sure they're what you were looking for.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T22:46:10-08:00","id":823087,"title":"","content":"I thought that the Unquenchable Flame was pretty cool. Not for the fact that you can <i>make</i> fire, but that rain <i>will not fall </i>within five feet of the fire. Somewhere, near the western pole, is an island constantly wracked by storms and infinite rain. Even in those inhospitable conditions, humans have settled, kept safe by sacred firepits. But their magic is old and weak, and several fires have been put out by neglect or wind. If only there was a thaumaturge to relight the fires and keep the village alive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:27:52-08:00","id":823541,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgies are not scientific and replicable. They are intuited. They are the product of magical thinking and improvisation and they do not work according to reasonable logical principles. For these reasons, I think Semicasual is on to something when he suggests stealing from Unknown Armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:53:26-08:00","id":823570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=823087#post823087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the Unquenchable Flame was pretty cool. Not for the fact that you can <i>make</i> fire, but that rain <i>will not fall </i>within five feet of the fire. Somewhere, near the western pole, is an island constantly wracked by storms and infinite rain. Even in those inhospitable conditions, humans have settled, kept safe by sacred firepits. But their magic is old and weak, and several fires have been put out by neglect or wind. If only there was a thaumaturge to relight the fires and keep the village alive...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm? Okay, THAT makes it cooler, I must have missed that little tidbit.<br /> <br /> (Though I AM a bit incredulous that apparently only one mortal knows this ritual. I can see Lookshy offering the person who knows this ritual all the comforts he could ask for if he'll just teach the ritual to a handful of students a day, so those new Thaumaturges can guarantee that the Lookshy camps always have working fires)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:47:54-08:00","id":823743,"title":"","content":"First off, the keyword there is &quot;apparently.&quot; Nobody's <i>found</i> a second person with it yet.<br /> <br /> Second, maybe they offered and he said no. Or maybe every time Lookshy goes looking for him, he hides in a cave because he doesn't want anything to do with them. Or maybe Lookshy isn't going to be assumed to have hundreds of thaumaturges at their beck and call, enough such for every army camp to have one of their own.<br /> <br /> Any way you cut it, it's just plain not implausible, so you can cut the incredulity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:09:35-08:00","id":823759,"title":"","content":"Lookshy is one of the few places I can imagine employing a large scale recruitment program for thaumaturges. Given their reach and pull in the Scavenger lands, and it being the most populous part of the Threshold, them having a couple hundred thaumaturges in their employ doesn't strike me as impossible.<br /> <br /> Of course, Sijan will be searching and recruiting in the same area...<br /> <br /> This is actually an interesting dilemma. As a thaumaturge in Bumfuck Nowhere, Scavenger Lands, you may be an important person, perhaps even the most important person around, but you're still in Bumfuck Nowhere. As a thaumaturge in the Seventh Legion or the Morticians' Order, you get the luxuries of civilization, but you'll never be as important as you were in your hometown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:26:44-08:00","id":824200,"title":"","content":"The trouble with &quot;If only there was a thaumaturge to keep the fires alive&quot; type stories is that specific thaumaturgies are supposed to be ultra-rare. Thaumaturges are &quot;rare,&quot; and most know only 1 ritual, and most will know unique rituals. The odds that your village gets the one specific thaumaturge they need are vanishingly small. The odds they do so repeatedly are statistically zero. It's way, way more likely to have an Exalt show up (particularly a Dragonblooded).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:09:08-08:00","id":824231,"title":"","content":"That assumes where Thaumaturges capable of performing a certain ritual manifests is completely random and there's already been indications that it's not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:25:44-08:00","id":824248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824200#post824200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trouble with &quot;If only there was a thaumaturge to keep the fires alive&quot; type stories is that specific thaumaturgies are supposed to be ultra-rare. Thaumaturges are &quot;rare,&quot; and most know only 1 ritual, and most will know unique rituals. The odds that your village gets the one specific thaumaturge they need are vanishingly small. The odds they do so repeatedly are statistically zero. It's way, way more likely to have an Exalt show up (particularly a Dragonblooded).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works - thaumaturges can teach and learn rituals between themselves.<br /> <br /> If there's a thaumaturgical ritual that's needed to relight the holy beacon warding your village against the Wyld, and a child is born with the ability to exorcise spirits, you take her to the current keeper of the holy beacon, and he can teach her - and learn exorcism in return, if he's so inclined.<br /> <br /> As long as you find gifted individuals willing to do whatever job you require of them, the rituals they have are safe - in fact, over the years, you can gather quite a living library of minor wonders!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:39:38-08:00","id":824381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824248#post824248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how it works - thaumaturges can teach and learn rituals between themselves.<br /> <br /> If there's a thaumaturgical ritual that's needed to relight the holy beacon warding your village against the Wyld, and a child is born with the ability to exorcise spirits, you take her to the current keeper of the holy beacon, and he can teach her - and learn exorcism in return, if he's so inclined.<br /> <br /> As long as you find gifted individuals willing to do whatever job you require of them, the rituals they have are safe - in fact, over the years, you can gather quite a living library of minor wonders!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which flies in the face of the supposed rarity of thaumaturges and the supposed paucity of their known rituals. You can't have something that can spread and be taught to something even as common as the Dragonblooded and have it be really that rare and hard-to-find.<br /> <br /> We're back, essentially, to thaumaturgy being minor sorceries that you need a merit to learn, which the book goes to extensive word-count to press the notion that this is precisely what it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:49:30-08:00","id":824389,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it WOULD have to be Dragonblooded that are thaumaturges or initiated into sorcery, which shouldn't really be all of them (or even a majority of them) by any stretch of the imagination. But I see your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:59:47-08:00","id":824397,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure when we defined thaumaturgists as rare, we didn't define the <i>exact</i> rarity. One would think that including the bit about teaching rituals suggests they're not defined as so rare as to not be able to pass on ritual knowledge across generations within a given (admittedly large) areas, as if that were the case, there wouldn't have been much point of including the bit about teaching rituals!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:59:59-08:00","id":824398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824381#post824381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which flies in the face of the supposed rarity of thaumaturges and the supposed paucity of their known rituals. You can't have something that can spread and be taught to something even as common as the Dragonblooded and have it be really that rare and hard-to-find.<br /> <br /> We're back, essentially, to thaumaturgy being minor sorceries that you need a merit to learn, which the book goes to extensive word-count to press the notion that this is precisely what it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two things I see here that make this a bit weird.<br /> <br /> One, while Dragon-Blooded are common, they're still rare. IN a world of half a billion people (likely more in 3e due to more space about), you still have Dragon-Blooded counted in the tens of thousands and tending to be centralized. In the Threshold, Dragon-Blooded are the most common sort of Exalt, but that's like saying that, say, a well is the most common sort of oasis in a desert. They're still rare in the grand scheme of deserts.<br /> <br /> We know thaumaturges are rare enough that you don't see one in every town and they are sought after. This means that many thaumaturges are probably like many outcaste Dragon-Blooded: singular heroes out in the boonies of the world. And likely due to the way Creation works as a mostly aggrarian society, many thaumaturges probably just don't do a lot to stand out. ANd there's likely a chance in a lot of cases indivdiuals who have prodigle powers never meet another one and when they do it's a recruitment system going out looking for them.<br /> <br /> I just don't see what's so weird about it to me I guess. Just because they can share rituals doesn't mean that there's some global network of minor sorcerers. The world is big and isolated enough to make such groups notable parts of some states, but not something I think you can just assume exists on the scales you are implying here.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:14:39-08:00","id":824413,"title":"","content":"I would basically shy away from using actual numbers because I'm terrible at them and any time I nail a population number down someone else who's better at them than me seizes on it and goes &quot;Aha, if that's true, then THIS IMPLICATION OF THAT must also be true&quot; and then goes on to treat that (unintended) implication as gospel, but here:<br /> <br /> Assume in sparsely-populated &quot;tribal&quot; areas where people tend to gather in groups of, oh, 150, there's like one thaumaturge every ten villages or something, with a new one usually coming along in time for the previous one to take as an apprentice. That is, any given population probably has access to one, but they're sparse enough that using that access may be a pain (unless you happen to be like the one village <i>right next</i> to the witch's hut). This probably means two thaumaturgist every 1,500 people in sparsely populated areas. As population density increases, the natural incidence of thaumaturgists decreases, purely because it's dumb for cities to have as many as that figure suggests. This is also probably inobvious or works on inobvious principles such that it is not possible for e.g. the Realm or Lookshy to deliberately set up a low-population area to &quot;farm&quot; for thaumaturgists to induct into some larger program like sohei-exorcists.<br /> <br /> This is going to hold up about as well to rigorous analysis as vampire population figures in <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> or <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>, i.e. hardly at all, and I don't care. If anyone wants to take a shot at a better set of numbers that achieve the same effect, go wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-05-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:16:46-08:00","id":824414,"title":"","content":"Essentially, thaumaturgy being an innate gift is there to prevent teaching it to everyone and their aunt as a way of mass-producing magic users. That's all there is to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:19:17-08:00","id":824416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824414#post824414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, thaumaturgy being an innate gift is there to prevent teaching it to everyone and their aunt as a way of mass-producing magic users. That's all there is to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to create an environment where more people who are believed to have magic and who make their living as witches are full of shit than actually have magic, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:20:23-08:00","id":824419,"title":"","content":"Is there a point to having the Thaumaturgy merit and not buying any ritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:21:02-08:00","id":824420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824419#post824419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a point to having the Thaumaturgy merit and not buying any ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to learn rituals later?<br /> <br /> It's honestly not costed for PC utility. Like, I think it's costed to get across the idea that it's not cost-effective and is therefore rare in-setting -- we don't want it to feel like an obvious choice during chargen. This is arguably not a great use of mechanics, but if we had made it a one-point Merit, the common wisdom would be &quot;Well why doesn't everyone take it?&quot; which is not the intended in-play effect. Assuming you're playing an Exalt, just learn sorcery if you want to have it for a reasonable cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 02-05-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:39:09-08:00","id":824431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824420#post824420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ability to learn rituals later?<br /> <br /> It's honestly not costed for PC utility. Like, I think it's costed to get across the idea that it's not cost-effective and is therefore rare in-setting -- we don't want it to feel like an obvious choice during chargen. This is arguably not a great use of mechanics, but if we had made it a one-point Merit, the common wisdom would be &quot;Well why doesn't everyone take it?&quot; which is not the intended in-play effect. Assuming you're playing an Exalt, just learn sorcery if you want to have it for a reasonable cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes much more sense. Thanks for the explanation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Though I'll admit that I am sad that the majority of mortals who say they have magic powers are frauds now. But that is something I can easily change in my own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:54:35-08:00","id":824450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824431#post824431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'll admit that I am sad that the majority of mortals who say they have magic powers are frauds now.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's bad about it?<br /> <br /> Not to tell you you're wrong to dislike it, but since I really like the idea, I'm curious of your reasoning for disliking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T11:23:53-08:00","id":824483,"title":"","content":"It's definitely a change. 2e's thaumaturgy took a lot of cues from Glorantha, which is a mythic fantasy setting takes the position &quot;In a magical setting, it would be cool if everyone could learn some small magics.&quot; And so you get e.g. nomadic herdsmen where the trick of creating fire with neither flint nor tinder is common and basically everyone in the world knows an effective ritual against misfortune or something. Glorantha is also a place where most people know the fundamentals of how magic and the world work.<br /> <br /> 3e very deliberately departs from that entirely. 3e Creation is a place where magic, though common, is much more often used to reinforce divisions of privilege and fortune than alleviate them, and superstition and misconception about how the world works is everywhere, leading to a ton of varying cultures all based on different worldviews. Varangian astrology, for example, is a bunch of oppressive nonsense idiosyncratic to Varang, that the Varangian people nevertheless invest a great deal of meaning into. It's not some special insight into the real astrology of the Five Maisens that's been applied culture-wide.<br /> <br /> See, as always, Tales of the Flat Earth for a fantasy setting where magic is real but weird and misunderstood.<br /> <br /> If you prefer a more Glorantha-like setup, 2e thaumaturgy is there for you to adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T12:14:51-08:00","id":824514,"title":"","content":"Upon thought, I want to revise my estimate of thaumaturgy's frequency even in sparse populations -- most of the time, the local person who's going to fulfill the role of &quot;witch&quot; will be someone with prayer skills and ties to the local gods, who works magic entirely indirectly via persuading divinities to do shit.<br /> <br /> I will, however, theorize that thaumaturgy is not evenly distributed. That is, in some bloodlines or populations or cultural traditions or maybe even just <i>places</i>, it's more common, and unbroken lines of tutelage can carry down culturally or pragmatically significant rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T12:28:16-08:00","id":824520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824514#post824514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon thought, I want to revise my estimate of thaumaturgy's frequency even in sparse populations -- most of the time, the local person who's going to fulfill the role of &quot;witch&quot; will be someone with prayer skills and ties to the local gods, who works magic entirely indirectly via persuading divinities to do shit.<br /> <br /> I will, however, theorize that thaumaturgy is not evenly distributed. That is, in some bloodlines or populations or cultural traditions or maybe even just <i>places</i>, it's more common, and unbroken lines of tutelage can carry down culturally or pragmatically significant rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the angle I've been taking during setting design, and the devs haven't taken the red pen to relevant references yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T13:18:41-08:00","id":824546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824483#post824483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Varangian astrology, for example, is a bunch of oppressive nonsense idiosyncratic to Varang, that the Varangian people nevertheless invest a great deal of meaning into. It's not some special insight into the real astrology of the Five Maidens that's been applied culture-wide..</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm thinking how fun it would be if someone with a gift got inducted into the ranks of astrologers and developed an actual ritual based on their practices - one that gave results widely different from what's expected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824514#post824514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will, however, theorize that thaumaturgy is not evenly distributed. That is, in some bloodlines or populations or cultural traditions or maybe even just <i>places</i>, it's more common, and unbroken lines of tutelage can carry down culturally or pragmatically significant rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm running with right now. In my planned Hundred Kingdoms game, there will be a kingdom where every firstborn daughter of the royal couple is a thaumaturge. Not quite sure where to go from here, but I like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T13:30:51-08:00","id":824556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824450#post824450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's bad about it?<br /> <br /> Not to tell you you're wrong to dislike it, but since I really like the idea, I'm curious of your reasoning for disliking it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824483#post824483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely a change. 2e's thaumaturgy took a lot of cues from Glorantha, which is a mythic fantasy setting takes the position &quot;In a magical setting, it would be cool if everyone could learn some small magics.&quot; And so you get e.g. nomadic herdsmen where the trick of creating fire with neither flint nor tinder is common and basically everyone in the world knows an effective ritual against misfortune or something. Glorantha is also a place where most people know the fundamentals of how magic and the world work.<br /> <br /> 3e very deliberately departs from that entirely. 3e Creation is a place where magic, though common, is much more often used to reinforce divisions of privilege and fortune than alleviate them, and superstition and misconception about how the world works is everywhere, leading to a ton of varying cultures all based on different worldviews. Varangian astrology, for example, is a bunch of oppressive nonsense idiosyncratic to Varang, that the Varangian people nevertheless invest a great deal of meaning into. It's not some special insight into the real astrology of the Five Maisens that's been applied culture-wide.<br /> <br /> See, as always, Tales of the Flat Earth for a fantasy setting where magic is real but weird and misunderstood.<br /> <br /> If you prefer a more Glorantha-like setup, 2e thaumaturgy is there for you to adapt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically what Stephen said. I like the idea that magic is built into the Framework of Creation. There is still room for superstition and fraud, but it is as rare as someone believing in a flat earth or embezzling money in the Real World.<br /> <br /> It's just a thematic different. I'll run games with a 2e view of magic. I'll run games with a 3e view of magic. My games are usually short term with a certain focus, so it will depend on what is needed for the story I want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:12:18-08:00","id":824573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824556#post824556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically what Stephen said. I like the idea that magic is built into the Framework of Creation. There is still room for superstition and fraud, but it is as rare as someone believing in a flat earth or embezzling money in the Real World.<br /> <br /> It's just a thematic different. I'll run games with a 2e view of magic. I'll run games with a 3e view of magic. My games are usually short term with a certain focus, so it will depend on what is needed for the story I want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever works for you. I did have my share of fun with 2e's take on thaumaturgy, but I like the new system more. Magic feels more... well, magical, when it's rare, shrouded in myth and superstition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:16:19-08:00","id":824580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824520#post824520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the angle I've been taking during setting design, and the devs haven't taken the red pen to relevant references yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are just busy playing Blade and Soul, give them time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:42:29-08:00","id":824665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824483#post824483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e very deliberately departs from that entirely. 3e Creation is a place where magic, though common, is much more often used to reinforce divisions of privilege and fortune than alleviate them, and superstition and misconception about how the world works is everywhere, leading to a ton of varying cultures all based on different worldviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. So, I apologize in advance for the tangent, but...this is always something that's made me raise an eyebrow about Exalted. I mean, it's certainly true to the source material, but a big thing that sold me on the game is the premise that You, The Protagonist have the power to make things <i>better</i>. That you don't have to settle for slapping a bandage on things by punching bad mans in the face until they go away, and can engage with the actual, underlying problems. Maybe you won't make everything better - maybe there's no solution that will satisfy everyone, or maybe you'll fuck up along the way - but the return of the Solars is meant to represent <i>hope</i> for Creation, and not just because the good kings are here to kick out all the bad ones.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask: in what way are player characters intended to address massive, systemic injustices? Injustices such as, say, entire geographical regions needing to keep a thaumaturge (or kidnap one, if there aren't any born to the native population) more or less prisoner to prevent the world from falling apart (I mean that one's straight out of Dark Souls with the Fire-Keepers, and DS is one of the most pessimistic settings that isn't Drakengard)? Or, for an example that's been around a lot longer, the Wavecrest Archipelago depending on industrial-scale human sacrifice to keep the volcano gods appeased?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:02:40-08:00","id":824678,"title":"","content":"Build an Artifact to replace the thaumaturge. Get an Eclipse to bind the volcano god to not put a gun to people's heads.<br /> <br /> The thing is that in this case, the two things you note are examples of just the world being a world that's not really fair and has some exotic dangerous shit. The aformentioned issue with the thaumaturge being obliged to protect her community is just something you see not just in fantasy but on Earth. And so solving that issue is finding a way to maybe convince the community that htey shouldn't put that on a person, or find a way that the community can do what it can without them. But you have to do so in a way that might be harder than just convicning people that their way of life is wrong. <br /> <br /> I guess to me the issue isn't that these situations aren't fixiable. Theya re. It's just they're not easy to fix. Which is I think something to think about with Creation compared to a more grimdark setup.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:23:21-08:00","id":824691,"title":"","content":"How can you expect us to write a setting that feels real, where addressing massive systemic injustice is simple?<br /> <br /> Like, I get this complaint <i>all the time:</i> &quot;Your setting acknowledges massive systemic injustice but doesn't provide players with the tools necessary to abolish it; it's such a <i>downer!&quot;</i> Uh... I don't know what to tell you, guy....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:25:15-08:00","id":824692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824691#post824691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you expect us to write a setting that feels real, where addressing massive systemic injustice is simple?</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow-up question: how do you make simple solutions to problems not boring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:26:07-08:00","id":824693,"title":"","content":"That's not what I asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:49:56-08:00","id":824709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824665#post824665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. So, I apologize in advance for the tangent, but...this is always something that's made me raise an eyebrow about Exalted. I mean, it's certainly true to the source material, but a big thing that sold me on the game is the premise that You, The Protagonist have the power to make things <i>better</i>. That you don't have to settle for slapping a bandage on things by punching bad mans in the face until they go away, and can engage with the actual, underlying problems. Maybe you won't make everything better - maybe there's no solution that will satisfy everyone, or maybe you'll fuck up along the way - but the return of the Solars is meant to represent <i>hope</i> for Creation, and not just because the good kings are here to kick out all the bad ones.<br /> <br /> So I have to ask: in what way are player characters intended to address massive, systemic injustices? Injustices such as, say, entire geographical regions needing to keep a thaumaturge (or kidnap one, if there aren't any born to the native population) more or less prisoner to prevent the world from falling apart (I mean that one's straight out of Dark Souls with the Fire-Keepers, and DS is one of the most pessimistic settings that isn't Drakengard)? Or, for an example that's been around a lot longer, the Wavecrest Archipelago depending on industrial-scale human sacrifice to keep the volcano gods appeased?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, to answer those specific scenarios, then:<br /> <br /> The dissolving edge of the world is often described in terms of there just not being enough people out there to reinforce reality sufficiently. Presumably those lands adjacent to the bordermarches could be made less twisted and less subject to the hungry Wyld if they were more fruitful and safe, so they could support larger populations. The <i>short-term</i> solution is inobvious because the edge of reality isn't going to stop crumbling until you get past a certain tipping point, but the long-term solution is to create a society with health, wealth, and happiness for all, at which point that fortune will serve as a bulwark against encroaching unreality. In the meantime, uh... you may need to keep the thaumaturgy going. Find volunteers? There have to be <i>some</i> people who have the gift of thaumaturgy for whom &quot;Learn mystic secrets and serve as the barrier between Is and Is Not&quot; is something like a calling.<br /> <br /> (Of course, that just means the lands next door are unstable, and somebody's gonna move in there eventually. Maybe break out the reality engines or, I dunno, bend the world into an eternal sphere so it has no edge. That last one seems pretty popular in actual play! This is a sort of long-term project.)<br /> <br /> Addressing the problem of the volcano gods usually just amounts to punching volcano gods and, again, raising up society to a sufficient level of health, wealth, and happiness that nobody is building their settlements within eruption range of volcanos. Modern Hawaii seems to do okay -- it's volcanically active and they just, uh, don't make anyone live where the lava will be. Again, this is an infrastructure problem -- if your society is structured such that you need rich volcanic soil to feed people, and your transportation is sufficiently bad the only way to reliably have access to it is to live close enough to the volcano that you'll die if it erupts, then you're in a bind, but it's not insoluble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T18:27:13-08:00","id":824724,"title":"","content":"Ah, good.<br /> <br /> To elaborate on where I'm coming from, it always seemed to me, ESPECIALLY in 2E, that virtually every problem in Creation had some magic-flavored but ultimately-technocratic solution...that RAN ON HUMAN BABIES. A particular, recurring case was &quot;Horrible supernatural tyrant who makes hard choices that other people won't, and deposing them will only lead to chaos&quot;. I think that the reason it was hard to call out the Perfect of Paragon as notably awful was that &quot;random mortal chances upon awesome supernatural power, founds Legalist dystopia with self as immortal God-Emperor for the greater good&quot; could easily describe <i>any given Solar </i>(seriously, I've seen SO MANY players decide that the only problem with the Realm was that <i>they </i>weren't in charge).<br /> <br /> The weird thing was that the writing kept asking &quot;But is violence <i>really </i>the answer, hmmm?&quot; in cases where yes, violence was very definitely the answer. Not to seem like I'm picking on you, personally, but I'm thinking of a hypothetical you raised in a thread about the role of priests in Creation. It involved a river god who kept demanding sex slaves in exchange for not flooding the farming villages along the river's banks, and how decent mortal priests would be able to bargain him down, while a Zenith would just threaten to murder him unless he fell in line, followed by an footnote that you really shouldn't do this because then there wouldn't be a god around to keep the river from flooding. This struck me as odd, mostly because of the constant debates over the material <i>importance </i>of gods. If the god cannot be slain without harming the river itself, then he enjoys an irreducible advantage in negotiations, and any deals you make (without an Eclipse bearing witness) will last exactly until you're out of earshot. If he <i>can</i>, then he's merely a rent-seeking parasite, and killing or sparing him - or <i>any </i>god - is purely a matter of political expedience. Unless you can actually bring him around to being less of a horrible person, to deal fairly with the villagers instead of regarding them as cattle, which is an option I hope will get more shrift over baby-based fuel economies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:27:55-08:00","id":824758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824724#post824724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing was that the writing kept asking &quot;But is violence <i>really </i>the answer, hmmm?&quot; in cases where yes, violence was very definitely the answer. Not to seem like I'm picking on you, personally, but I'm thinking of a hypothetical you raised in a thread about the role of priests in Creation. It involved a river god who kept demanding sex slaves in exchange for not flooding the farming villages along the river's banks, and how decent mortal priests would be able to bargain him down, while a Zenith would just threaten to murder him unless he fell in line, followed by an footnote that you really shouldn't do this because then there wouldn't be a god around to keep the river from flooding. This struck me as odd, mostly because of the constant debates over the material <i>importance </i>of gods. If the god cannot be slain without harming the river itself, then he enjoys an irreducible advantage in negotiations, and any deals you make (without an Eclipse bearing witness) will last exactly until you're out of earshot. If he <i>can</i>, then he's merely a rent-seeking parasite, and killing or sparing him - or <i>any </i>god - is purely a matter of political expedience. Unless you can actually bring him around to being less of a horrible person, to deal fairly with the villagers instead of regarding them as cattle, which is an option I hope will get more shrift over baby-based fuel economies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The river and the river's god are two separate things. It's quite possible to kill the god without causing the river to flood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:48:44-08:00","id":824767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanandithras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824758#post824758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The river and the river's god are two separate things. It's quite possible to kill the god without causing the river to flood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. But on the other hand, the god does have a valuable job; it's not just a parasite with no function other than to fuck with mortals. Its job is to observe when things happen to the river outside of the river's current destiny\u2014which is rare, and can be the work of supernatural forces, unpredictable mortals, or just random chance\u2014and correct the problem if possible, or call for more puissant divine aid for problems beyond its capabilities to handle. (Though the latter is often impossible due to the decay of the Terrestrial spirit courts.) If the river floods when it isn't supposed to, or it's contaminated such that everyone in the village will catch cholera, it's the god's responsibility to report the matter up the chain, and to intervene if it's capable.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if Heaven has decided that half the village will die of cholera, it's also the god's job to make sure that no one cleans up that pesky contamination in the water. Suddenly, the desirability of a corrupt, apathetic, incompetent, or weak god\u2014as opposed to one dedicated to its intended purpose\u2014changes considerably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":1120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","user":"Eric Minton","date":". 02-05-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T04:30:37-08:00","id":824896,"title":"","content":"So, having +1'd wonderandawe, here's a question:<br /> <br /> Why is Speak With Ozashun thaumaturgy? Like, I can see why Second Bread or Exorcism are thaumaturgy, but this feels more like it has more to do with Ozashun that with the thaumaturge.<br /> <br /> I mean, sacrificing innocents to Alveua to have yourself reforged isn't thaumaturgy, and invoking the Pale Mistress to fuck up a ghost isn't thaumaturgy (I hope). What makes &quot;Ozashun will give secret knowledge in return for access to children's dreams&quot; thaumaturgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T17:58:07-08:00","id":825167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824896#post824896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, having +1'd wonderandawe, here's a question:<br /> <br /> Why is Speak With Ozashun thaumaturgy? Like, I can see why Second Bread or Exorcism are thaumaturgy, but this feels more like it has more to do with Ozashun that with the thaumaturge.<br /> <br /> I mean, sacrificing innocents to Alveua to have yourself reforged isn't thaumaturgy, and invoking the Pale Mistress to fuck up a ghost isn't thaumaturgy (I hope). What makes &quot;Ozashun will give secret knowledge in return for access to children's dreams&quot; thaumaturgy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, Ozashun isn't something you can just pray to or otherwise gain its attention without the ritual. Alternatively, the ritual guarantees you success in ways that prayer doesn't - you keep doing the same thing and getting the same result. Something which may or may not be possible with other supernatural beings, but sure is handy when available, especially for mortals who don't get much of an edge when it comes to bargaining. I mean, it's not like whatever you do is guaranteed to gain Alveua's attention unless you have Demon of the Second Circle on hand.<br /> <br /> On a more general note, it's an example of a ritual that's tied to a specific place and a magical issue. It shows what weird shit can happen in Creation, and how thaumaturgy factors into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:36:36-08:00","id":825968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824413#post824413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would basically shy away from using actual numbers because I'm terrible at them and any time I nail a population number down someone else who's better at them than me seizes on it and goes &quot;Aha, if that's true, then THIS IMPLICATION OF THAT must also be true&quot; and then goes on to treat that (unintended) implication as gospel, but here:<br /> <br /> Assume in sparsely-populated &quot;tribal&quot; areas where people tend to gather in groups of, oh, 150, there's like one thaumaturge every ten villages or something, with a new one usually coming along in time for the previous one to take as an apprentice. That is, any given population probably has access to one, but they're sparse enough that using that access may be a pain (unless you happen to be like the one village <i>right next</i> to the witch's hut). This probably means two thaumaturgist every 1,500 people in sparsely populated areas. As population density increases, the natural incidence of thaumaturgists decreases, purely because it's dumb for cities to have as many as that figure suggests. This is also probably inobvious or works on inobvious principles such that it is not possible for e.g. the Realm or Lookshy to deliberately set up a low-population area to &quot;farm&quot; for thaumaturgists to induct into some larger program like sohei-exorcists.<br /> <br /> This is going to hold up about as well to rigorous analysis as vampire population figures in <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> or <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i>, i.e. hardly at all, and I don't care. If anyone wants to take a shot at a better set of numbers that achieve the same effect, go wild.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a FAR more common spread of them than I got from reading the entry in the Ex3 core book, but does make the idea that thaumaturgy is worth its space in the book more palatable. Though it still kind-of feels like it's back to being &quot;folk magic&quot; rather than &quot;incredibly rare miracles,&quot; I think that's where it SHOULD be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T14:36:21-08:00","id":828438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824431#post824431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes much more sense. Thanks for the explanation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I'll admit that I am sad that the majority of mortals who say they have magic powers are frauds now. But that is something I can easily change in my own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you'd need to change it.<br /> I've never seen an Exalted game where the extreme unlikelyhood of running into other Exalts let alone ones you've got past life history with was seriously given the time of day. In just the same way you don't need to waste the PCs time with the charlatans just because there's more of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:20:57-08:00","id":828465,"title":"","content":"I don't think the word &quot;fraud&quot; paints an accurate picture of the majority of Creation's occultists. You can believe in a ritual (perhaps at one point passed to you by an actual thaumaturgist) and your power to perform it, and you can perform it to people's benefit rather than to cynically scam them.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine a girl whose grandma was a gifted tea leaves reader, and who was trained in the art but didn't inherit the gift. The ritual involves actually looking at tea leaves and divining meaning from their pattern, and the girl may very well believe she's seeing the future, because Grandma showed her various patterns and explained what they mean (or rather, what they meant to her, but the girl doesn't necessarily have to grasp that nuance). Presumably, being a successful diviner takes a lot of social skill and guesswork even if you can actually see the future (for a real life analogue, consider many brilliant scientists who nevertheless make poor science communicators), and the girl can easily get that part done very well. End result is, you get someone who's good at giving advice, and people are inclined to listen because they believe she's actually a seer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:25:03-08:00","id":828469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=828465#post828465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the word &quot;fraud&quot; paints an accurate picture of the majority of Creation's occultists. You can believe in a ritual (perhaps at one point passed to you by an actual thaumaturgist) and your power to perform it, and you can perform it to people's benefit rather than to cynically scam them.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine a girl whose grandma was a gifted tea leaves reader, and who was trained in the art but didn't inherit the gift. The ritual involves actually looking at tea leaves and divining meaning from their pattern, and the girl may very well believe she's seeing the future, because Grandma showed her various patterns and explained what they mean (or rather, what they meant to her, but the girl doesn't necessarily have to grasp that nuance). Presumably, being a successful diviner takes a lot of social skill and guesswork even if you can actually see the future (for a real life analogue, consider many brilliant scientists who nevertheless make poor science communicators), and the girl can easily get that part done very well. End result is, you get someone who's good at giving advice, and people are inclined to listen because they believe she's actually a seer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=825968#post825968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a FAR more common spread of them than I got from reading the entry in the Ex3 core book, but does make the idea that thaumaturgy is worth its space in the book more palatable. Though it still kind-of feels like it's back to being &quot;folk magic&quot; rather than &quot;incredibly rare miracles,&quot; I think that's where it SHOULD be.</div> </div> </div> </div>See my followup post -- I was overestimating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T10:27:02-08:00","id":829792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824556#post824556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that magic is built into the Framework of Creation. There is still room for superstition and fraud, but it is as rare as someone believing in a flat earth or embezzling money in the Real World.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this is that the characters most likely to assume that the fortune teller is a fraud are the PCs, specifically the ones whose players intend for their character to be educated or at least worldly. Now they come across as stupid or paranoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:09:51-08:00","id":830024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=829792#post829792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with this is that the characters most likely to assume that the fortune teller is a fraud are the PCs, specifically the ones whose players intend for their character to be educated or at least worldly. Now they come across as stupid or paranoid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would a worldly PC think a Fortune Teller was a fraud if Fortune Telling is real in the setting? I would use a Fortune Teller NPC to give PCs hints or have the NPC killed by the antagonist for knowing too much. I usually save my shady NPCs for the Bureaucrats. <br /> <br /> Eh. I think I am more flexible about how would be portrayed in my Exalted games than most people on the forums. I got into the game right when Dreams of the First Age came out, so my point of view is skewed towards the crazy anime magitech Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T23:32:26-08:00","id":830061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=830024#post830024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a worldly PC think a Fortune Teller was a fraud if Fortune Telling is real in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because frauds are <i>also</i> a thing in the setting.<br /> <br /> Doctors are real in our world, you know, but that doesn't mean everyone who calls herself one can be trusted to give medical advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-15-2016, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T02:10:21-08:00","id":830104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">as rare as someone believing in a flat earth or embezzling money in the Real World.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, what? Is that capitalization meant to be referring to the MTV reality show? If not, what exactly makes you think embezzlement is notably rare? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a worldly PC think a Fortune Teller was a fraud if Fortune Telling is real in the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div> Familiarity with how rare the ability to tell fortunes actually is combined with familiarity with how commonly somebody can get away with pretending they have it for profit. I wouldn't even compare it to doctors, if only because that's a highly regulated profession (even if some more fradulent positions such as nutritionists can still get by with false credentials, they're just a bit tangential); it's more like, say, nannies or day care managers, a job in which, last I heard, regulations in parts of the U.S. are still so lax that unless you're the kind of person who might read reports on inquiries into it, you wouldn't be able to tell on the face of it just how many people are operating without any kind of child-caring qualifications, and the really shoddy services that operate as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T06:57:59-08:00","id":830211,"title":"","content":"The idea that a huge number of people in 2e Creation had knowledge of individual Thaumaturgy Rituals is basically fanon. As far as Oadenol's Codex and Scroll of Heroes were concerned a Thaumaturge was someone who had Degrees and would be a full blown spell caster in a more Dungeons and Dragons derived setting, the archetypes present in the Codex even resemble adventurer classes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-15-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:03:07-08:00","id":830229,"title":"","content":"*snrk* The idea that government regulations on things as small-scale as babysitting actually do anything to improve the quality of service provided (rather than just make it more expensive and exclusive to big businesses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:02:48-08:00","id":831331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> things as small-scale as babysitting</div> </div> </div> </div> Do I need to explain the difference between having somebody in the same house as a sleeping child for a couple of hours and full-time professional childcare? Do I need to explain why some regulation of the care service provided for some of the most vulnerable human beings there are might be a halfway desirable thing? I know that I do, but it's still a depressing reality to acknowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:34:38-08:00","id":831819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=831331#post831331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do I need to explain the difference between having somebody in the same house as a sleeping child for a couple of hours and full-time professional childcare? Do I need to explain why some regulation of the care service provided for some of the most vulnerable human beings there are might be a halfway desirable thing? I know that I do, but it's still a depressing reality to acknowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do I need to explain that the government is woefully inadequate to the task, and tends to have priorities more set in place by larger businesses seeking to keep competition out of the market than any actual care for the people it's supposedly acting on behalf of?<br /> <br /> There are other, better mechanisms; this is, however, not the thread to discuss it. (And if you don't want to have your political views challenged, don't inject them into these threads.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T10:25:13-08:00","id":831853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=831819#post831819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And if you don't want to have your political views challenged, don't inject them into these threads.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T11:14:51-08:00","id":832616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I need to explain that the government is woefully inadequate to the task</div> </div> </div> </div>How are people licensed to practice law or medicine? Drive cars?<br /> <br /> Although that's probably getting off track; even if one is so cynical as to assume that it is impossible to license and regulate professional child caring, one still winds up with a situation in which the existence of individuals and businesses with actual qualifications does not preclude people from being basically defrauded by folks who will leave their infants in a room unsupervised and sitting in their own excrement.<br /> <br /> Perhaps an example that is more overt... I would find the assumption that actual fortune tellers existing precludes people from being defrauded to hold as much water as the assumption of decent, qualified care facilities for the elderly precludes anybody from unknowingly leaving their relatives in hell holes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you don't want to have your political views challenged, don't inject them into these threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:20:58-08:00","id":832657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=832616#post832616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are people licensed to practice law or medicine? Drive cars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Law, medicine, and driving are all high-visibility activities. &quot;Professional&quot; child care can easily be some lady who takes money to watch your kids while you are at work. It is too easy for these cases to fall through cracks in the system. Then, of course, is what would licensing even consist of? Knowing how to change a diaper? How to call 911 in the event of an emergency? Further, a license does not preclude operational malfeasance - one can have a food handler's permit and still forget to wash and sanitize properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps an example that is more overt... I would find the assumption that actual fortune tellers existing precludes people from being defrauded to hold as much water as the assumption of decent, qualified care facilities for the elderly precludes anybody from unknowingly leaving their relatives in hell holes. </div> </div> </div>Except the &quot;hell holes&quot; are the minority of facilities and they trade on the good reputation that the legitimate facilities have - the odds of picking something understaffed, unqualified, or plain malicious is against you. With fortune telling, we're looking at the majority being frauds. How does the legitimate fortune teller distinguish himself to the PCs? How do the PCs decide that the charlatans are charlatans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:28:04-08:00","id":832663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821654#post821654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope I'm not the only one interested in actually devising thaumaturgical gifts, here.<br /> <br /> <br /> * You can summon the ghosts of people who are recently departed, allowing them to possess your body for a short time while another person talks to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semicasual, I ended up using this Gift for an NPC in my Ex3 game. It just made sense for a Mortal Inspector to have that ability. Of course this NPC doesn't like using it, but the Dragonblooded he works for loves that he has it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:54:53-08:00","id":832694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=832663#post832663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Semicasual, I ended up using this Gift for an NPC in my Ex3 game. It just made sense for a Mortal Inspector to have that ability. Of course this NPC doesn't like using it, but the Dragonblooded he works for loves that he has it. </div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I remembered that trick from Rashomon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:42:24-08:00","id":833076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=832616#post832616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are people licensed to . . . [d]rive cars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incompetently. There's a reason why new drivers are charged <i>massively</i> higher rates for insurance, and it certainly isn't because the licensing requirements actually make sure that new drivers can competently drive cars in traffic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T08:03:15-08:00","id":833271,"title":"","content":"One interesting thing is that the system definitely supports dragonblooded as being the &quot;Best&quot; at thaumaturgy, if for nothing else than their lifespan.<br /> <br /> Only a group long enough lived and wealthy enough to create living libraries of thaumaturges can really excel at it. I'm really seeing the schools for dragonblooded as almost like a retirement home/technical school, which crotchety old thaumaturges who all know dozens upon dozens of skills who are protected as living treasures. Students can learn specific skills from the old masters, who's main job is to teach and preserve the rituals deemed important. However to &quot;earn&quot; a position as a &quot;master&quot; (i'm seeing this kinda like old school oxford) a student has to go out into creation to find a new ritual worth adding to the ranks of the school. A Thaumaturgical skill to make moss grow is fairly useless, a Ritual to change the color of cloth is not.<br /> <br /> thaumaturgy seems really really close to the magic in the &quot;Legend of Nightfall&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is honestly all i need for a good mortal seed game. A group of Young students combing the outer reaches of the empire, looking for someone with a knack that they can bring back and earn their robes, maybe someone exalts? maybe &quot;who knows what happens&quot;?<br /> <br /> It really depends on how long it takes to learn a ritual and what level of personal teaching it takes, one at a time? classroom style?<br /> Does it take a week, or a month, or a year to learn a ritual?<br /> <br /> Just to make it easier i'll probably steal the guidelines from mage the awakening, a one dot thaumaturgy ritual gets you anything a 1 dot mage could do (pick a one dot rote, or something of equal power) and a two dot ritual gets you a 2 dot mage rote/equivalent. yeah it'll take a little conversion, but it saves me the trouble of making something up whole cloth.<br /> <br /> For example i can totally see the Funerists knowing and keeping a 2 dot ritual that does the same thing as Corpse mask (MtA) or Ghost Summon<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5303-lokiyn","name":"Lokiyn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:14:32-08:00","id":835018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=833076#post833076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incompetently. There's a reason why new drivers are charged <i>massively</i> higher rates for insurance, and it certainly isn't because the licensing requirements actually make sure that new drivers can competently drive cars in traffic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is off topic, and I really am not trying to prolong the debate, but that's an interesting thought: what if all it took to drive legally was personal auto insurance? That is, proof that you're insured, personally?<br /> <br /> I imagine auto insurance companies would still charge a lot more for inexperienced drivers, but they may also actually institute tests of their own to rate clients for various safety levels. I could also see insurance being &quot;for the vehicle&quot; (particularly expensive if the authorized driver list is not restrictive) or being &quot;personal&quot; (you pay the insurance company to insure you on any vehicle you drive, or on a particular class of vehicles you drive).<br /> <br /> ...anyway, sorry, tangent. That just seemed an interesting alternate solution to the &quot;who gets to drive?&quot; problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:45:57-08:00","id":835046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=833271#post833271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One interesting thing is that the system definitely supports dragonblooded as being the &quot;Best&quot; at thaumaturgy, if for nothing else than their lifespan.</div> </div> </div> </div>DBs can only access thaumaturgy reliably if they're sorcerers - while nothing specifically precludes a DB from being born with the gift of thaumaturgy, its overal rarity coupled with relatively low numbers of DBs in the world doesn't really support there being more than a handful of &quot;natural&quot; DB thaumaturgists.<br /> <br /> I'd presume most DB sorcerers will consider the pursuit of thaumaturgy somewhat beneath their level. Some scholars of the Heptagram will no doubt find special interest in it, but on the whole, learning actual sorcery will be considered a much better investment of students' time and effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:31:25-08:00","id":835379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=835018#post835018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is off topic, and I really am not trying to prolong the debate, but that's an interesting thought: what if all it took to drive legally was personal auto insurance? That is, proof that you're insured, personally?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too much. Most of what you suggested exists to one degree or another under the current system in the US, depending on state insurance regulations and costs to the insurers to implement. See Progressive's Snapshot for a example of using modern tech to inexpensively test clients' actual driving proficiency.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:39:07-07:00","id":962666,"title":"","content":"Found another cool one - cool enough to justify resurrecting the thread.<br /> <br /> * You were born blind, but you learned how to see through the eyes of other people near you - within 50 feet or so. Other people in your family can only do it when they're standing still with their eyes closed - you, and you alone, can &quot;sight-jack&quot; while you walk or do other tasks. You're used to seeing yourself from a second-person perspective, and can perform complicated hand-eye coordination tasks if another person is watching you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T01:46:25-07:00","id":962741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=833271#post833271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really depends on how long it takes to learn a ritual and what level of personal teaching it takes, one at a time? classroom style?<br /> Does it take a week, or a month, or a year to learn a ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgic rituals are specified as needing to be passed on through one-on-one practical tutoring. A rituallist could <i>possibly </i>mentor several students at once, but with diminished returns.<br /> <br /> Training Times, on pages 178-9, don't include rituals, but it takes one week per new rating for a (purchased) Merit, and two weeks per Circle for a spell. I'd lean towards the former for rituals (which also follow the dot rating model). <i>Edit:</i> Page 490 discusses the cost and training time for thaumaturgy and it is indeed one week per dot rating; 3xp for a one dot ritual, 5xp for a two dot ritual.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, for player characters with <b>xp </b>on hand (or a charm like Dark Minder's Observance). NPC may like to take things at a more relaxed pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:59:14-08:00","id":1045038,"title":"","content":"I've got a new edition of Unknown Armies, and that means.... new rituals!<br /> <br /> * You can coax an immaterial spirit into a living human body by driving a metal spike through the parietal bone of their skull while reciting a chant. This is more challenging than it sounds - if you kill the human outright, the ritual fails. Thus, using some kind of drill is recommended.<br /> <br /> * If you hold someone's head beneath the water until bubbles stop coming to the surface, they do not drown. Instead, they become able to breath in water for a few weeks.<br /> <br /> * You can make black mirrors that show a person's true face, both in the figurative and mystical sense.<br /> <br /> * Do not eat or drink anything but water for three days and nights. Lie facedown on the ground for a few minutes, then get up as quickly as you can and spin around counterclockwise. You will have visions of important events transpiring in Yu-Shan. The gods may notice you doing this, and give you unusually good or bad luck for several days afterwards.<br /> <br /> * Draw a straight line in white on your (or another person's) face, starting where your left earlobe attaches, passing through the left corner of your left eye. Do the same with a red line from right earlobe and right eye. Then, stick a silver needle in the place where the lines meet while concentrating on a memory. You will re-experience the events of that memory with perfect clarity, &quot;refreshing&quot; your knowledge of it as though it had happened less than an hour ago.<br /> <br /> * Draw a complex mandala pattern, then sit in the middle of it and lick the skin of a psychoactive amphibian. For a few minutes, you gain the ability to &quot;Measure the Wind&quot; (as the charm), and subconsciously use it on everything you can see - which includes all manner of small gods and any invisible, immaterial beings in your presence. You can also spot Dragon Lines, if you happen to be near one.<br /> <br /> * You can erode someone's Intimacy toward a specific person in their lives with the gift of a carved wooden doll. As long as they keep the doll, that intimacy degrades by one rank each week, until it is all-but-forgotten. Destroying the doll undoes the spell.<br /> <br /> * You can convert old, misused carriages into ghost traps.<br /> <br /> * You can make magical amulets with a bunch of nice-smelling ingredients - ambergris, orange peel, cloves - that help prevent people from becoming sick.<br /> <br /> * You can make a special cake with three ounces of human blood. Supposedly, eating the whole thing will prevent evil spirits from haunting you, but in reality what it does is relieve anxiety - like magical Prozac. Consumption of the blood cake gives the consumer three days of relief from all manner of phobias and background stress.<br /> <br /> * You know a chant that induces an ASMR response in anyone you speak it to. Some people find it relaxing or pleasurable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-07-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:56:55-08:00","id":1045179,"title":"","content":"<i>- Ligier-Repelling Veil: </i>By wearing a white veil over your head, spirits and Fair Folk will assume that the character has the Hideous Merit.<br /> <br /> <i>- Borrowed Luck: </i>The thaumaturgists ties coins to a red string and lend it to a child. Creature of darkness and Fair Folk will have trouble noticing the kid, but it becomes easier for them to detect the thaumaturgists.<br /> <br /> <i>- False Yin-Yang Eyes: </i>Dip a strawdoll's head into the blood of ink black dog, then nailed it under someone bed. The target will see hallucinations of ghost. Knowing the victim date of birth and tying a locket of their hair into the strawdoll increase the effect.<br /> <br /> <i>- Boat of Passage: </i>Put a lotus flower-shaped lantern along with something significant to the dead on a paper boat then release it on a river, the ghost of the decease will feel an strong urge to enter the cycle of reincarnation. The paper boat unnaturally crosses to the other side of river despite the water current. At higher tier, any ghosts who can see the lantern light will feel the same urge.<br /> <br /> <i>- Urrrghblaarrgh, Rice !!!??: </i>Against Creature of Dead, white rice gains the stat of a Light thrown weapon with the Lethal and Throw (Short) tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-07-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:11:24-08:00","id":1045374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=962741#post962741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgic rituals are specified as needing to be passed on through one-on-one practical tutoring. A rituallist could <i>possibly </i>mentor several students at once, but with diminished returns.<br /> <br /> Training Times, on pages 178-9, don't include rituals, but it takes one week per new rating for a (purchased) Merit, and two weeks per Circle for a spell. I'd lean towards the former for rituals (which also follow the dot rating model).<br /> <br /> This is, of course, for player characters with <b>xp </b>on hand (or a charm like Dark Minder's Observance). NPC may like to take things at a more relaxed pace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> perhaps worth noting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Third Edition, p. 490</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character with the Thaumaturgist Merit may learn thaumaturgic rituals. One-dot rituals cost three experience points to learn. These rituals represent the simplest and purest ritual magic available. Two-dot rituals are slightly more complex or difficult, and cost five experience points to learn. Training time for a thaumaturgy ritual is (dot rating) weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rational for the Merit supposition is that one-dot rituals cost an equivalent amount to a single dot in a Merit in EXP. Training time is listed here rather than with the other training times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:01:17-08:00","id":1046090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=821563#post821563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and hundreds of sorcerers (at minimum) who can call down bread from heaven sufficient to feed a village.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but can they? That spell isn't one that's been adapted to 3e, due to either wordcount or not having a discernable control spell effect.<br /> I'm not bitter :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T22:15:51-08:00","id":1046180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1046090#post1046090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but can they?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're unlikely to get a reply from Segev here; the poster you're addressing was banned some months ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:27:13-08:00","id":1046353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1046180#post1046180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're unlikely to get a reply from Segev here; the poster you're addressing was banned some months ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh.<br /> Well, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T16:31:44-08:00","id":1046517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=817641#post817641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea it looks like glorified mutations for now. Im going to wait for the magic book? If thats a thing? Maybe theyll elaborate on it. For now it looks like its just thier to keep the term for brand recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say more like channeling and exploting little, peculiar bugs in the tapestry of fate, so to speak. Maybe it's just me, but i associate them a little with minor Paradox or weird causality faults related to fate damage that we would get some mentions of in Sidereal-related stuff.<br /> <br /> Anyway, speaking about the OP's request for healing thaumaturgy - and forgive if some else has already suggested that - what about expelling a disease through exorcism rituals?<br /> <br /> Just replace &quot;a difficulty of the ghost/demons\u2019s Essence and a goal number of its Willpower,&quot; with &quot;Morbidity&quot; for diff. &amp; &quot;Morbidity + Virulence&quot; or &quot;Morbidity x2&quot; for goal and you're mostly set to go. One could even extrapolate things and maybe use the 2-dot ritual to <i>imprison a disease <b>and its spirit</b></i> in some sealed statue or object. Sounds ok for you people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=824546#post824546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm thinking how fun it would be if someone with a gift got inducted into the ranks of astrologers and developed an actual ritual based on their practices - one that gave results widely different from what's expected.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's what I'm running with right now. In my planned Hundred Kingdoms game, there will be a kingdom where every firstborn daughter of the royal couple is a thaumaturge. Not quite sure where to go from here, but I like the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only having boys could become something of a serious social/state issue.<br /> <br /> And if the royal couple get replaced by some branch of relatives that already have girls, does it means their existing firstborn gains &quot;the gift&quot;, the firstborn daughter <b>after</b> their proclamation as new royal couple or both?<br /> <br /> And how does one find out for sure?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens if someone of either royal couple - deposed or current - had a child out of wedlock, with a member of a foreign (but still royal technically) house, to further complicate matters?<br /> <br /> Just some quick, silly ideas that came out of your concept. How does that work out for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-09-2017, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:16:17-08:00","id":1046777,"title":"","content":"<i>- Silence of the Lamb: </i>Putting a white piece of cloth over a baby's face will make it stops crying.<br /> <br /> <i>- Moon-Viewing Flower:</i> As long as the front of your body faces toward the sky and it's night time, you can not sink in water. A higher dot version allows this to work at day time.<br /> <br /> <i>- Fireflies Under the Ocean</i>: Your movement underwater leaves a trail of glowing blue light. Ghosts is attracted to this display of luminescence.<br /> <br /> <i>- Bride of Nine Springs:</i> You don't need to eat, drink or breath, and your body won't product any waste if you stays submerged in a naturally-occurring large or moving body of water (an ocean or river counts, a bathing pool won't), you also immune to any water-based hazard like cold or pressure. If you continuously benefited from this Merit for three days straight then from the fourth day, the ST rolls one dice, failure means you get get transport to one of the Underworld's nine springs.<br /> <br /> <i>- Gnawing on Siren Song:</i> The thaumaturgists can store human teeth in some kind of container (pendant, jar,...etc). She can increase her Resolve against the mental magic of Fair Folk, each points increased causes one tooth in the container to decay.<br /> <br /> <i>- Womb of Drowned-Twin</i>: A person with this Merit can gleam someone thought and emotion, as long as both are in physical contact and is submerged under water. This is a two-way street method, since the other person can do the same thing even if they lack the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-10-2017, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:21:19-08:00","id":1046783,"title":"","content":"Jen these are very cool, but I have to ask...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1046777#post1046777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>- Moon-Viewing Flower:</i> As long as the front of your body faces toward the sky and it's night time, <b>you can't not sink </b>in water. A higher dot version allows this to work at day time.</div> </div> </div> </div>...does this mean you <i>always </i>sink? Or are you trying to say you always <i>float</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:30:06-08:00","id":1046786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1046783#post1046783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jen these are very cool, but I have to ask...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...does this mean you <i>always </i>sink? Or are you trying to say you always <i>float</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh, it's the later. Thanks TUH, I'll fix it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:09:00-08:00","id":1049946,"title":"","content":"Weather working, there's an art of which most rituals might make good fodder to port over to 3e, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:58:19-08:00","id":1049971,"title":"","content":"I think that weather-working as a thaumaturgy ritual in 3rd edition merits careful consideration. It would certainly be useful to people in Creation, but would it be good for the setting for them to have it? Or perhaps put another way, are they actually interesting and not just useful?<br /> <br /> If I were to convert them to the 3rd edition, I would look at different pieces and I would try to consider how to make them peculiar and interesting and strange. At least, moreso than they may have already been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:15:16-08:00","id":1049980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1049971#post1049971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that weather-working as a thaumaturgy ritual in 3rd edition merits careful consideration. It would certainly be useful to people in Creation, but would it be good for the setting for them to have it? Or perhaps put another way, are they actually interesting and not just useful?</div> </div> </div> </div>PLENTY of potential role-playing fodder to be had in weather-working magic, specially when it puts you at cross-purposes with the courts of the Wind Masters, as implied sometimes in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1049971#post1049971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to convert them to the 3rd edition, I would look at different pieces and I would try to consider how to make them peculiar and interesting and strange. At least, moreso than they may have already been.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for certain - part of the reason for doing away with the old arts system of thaumaturgy was most certainly to break away from a certain standardization/banalization of the rituals it seemed to foster to no small degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T12:23:13-08:00","id":1049988,"title":"","content":"While antagonizing weather gods is all well and good, I was thinking about how it could influence socio-political situations in Creation by a huge degree, because weather is like one of the more determining factors of how people live or die and how kingdoms rise and fall. It can be cool for a story, but an overabundance might deform the setting a tad.<br /> <br /> Though, I suppose that point is a little moot when we think about how rare such an ability might be, especially in the context of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should instead frame this as more of an anxiety than any kind of injunction against it. If it's cool and got great flavor, I think I could be down with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:00:07-08:00","id":1050043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1049988#post1049988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While antagonizing weather gods is all well and good, I was thinking about how it could influence socio-political situations in Creation by a huge degree, because weather is like one of the more determining factors of how people live or die and how kingdoms rise and fall. It can be cool for a story, but an overabundance might deform the setting a tad.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is something of a matter for thaumaturgy &amp; its degree of relative rarity as a whole not weather-working in particular i guess. And getting the attention of air elementals and weather gods has ups &amp; downs all its own one might require far more than thaumaturgy to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1049988#post1049988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I suppose that point is a little moot when we think about how rare such an ability might be, especially in the context of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should instead frame this as more of an anxiety than any kind of injunction against it. If it's cool and got great flavor, I think I could be down with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Overall i tend to think of thaumaturgists in terms of people will cool peculiar supernatural gifts like one might see in Inu-Yasha, Blue Exorcist, Mushishi and other series with similar &quot;supernatural exploration&quot; themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-08-2017, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T06:06:07-07:00","id":1126274,"title":"","content":"Been reading some Sam Sykes recently, and I got an idea for a ritual cool enough to justify thread-necromancy:<br /> <br /> There is a ritual so little-known as to be performed by accident more often than on purpose. It is, however, very powerful - it can grant any mortal the ability to see and kill any spirit, even if they are impervious to mortal weapons.<br /> <br /> A viable target for the ritual must first possess three things - gods, a family, and a home. They must then lose all of these things.<br /> <br /> The &quot;gods&quot; part is easiest in some ways, in that is mostly abstract. It is not necessary kill all the gods that the target worships, only that the target stops worshiping them. Cursory acknowledgment of their existence is permitted in the absence of fear, reverence, or respect. The preferred result is for the target to believe that gods are <i>unworthy</i> of worship.<br /> <br /> The &quot;family&quot; consists of everyone the target considers to be family, regardless of whether they are blood relatives or the degree of closeness. Every member of this family must die.<br /> <br /> The &quot;home&quot; consists of the personal dwelling of the target as well as anything they have that is familiar enough to be a &quot;second home.&quot; The home must be burned - specifically, burned. No other method of destruction will satisfy the ritual.<br /> <br /> When the target has lost everything - they have no gods, no family, and no home - and they sift through the ashes of their home, they will find a mundane iron, steel, or bronze sword. If they lose it, they will shortly after find another one. As long as they possess any sword, they can deal lethal damage even to creatures that would normally be immune. Also, If they did not have at least three dots in the Melee Ability already, they gain up to that amount. These blessings last as long as the target lives.<br /> <br /> This ritual does not confer any other Abilities, Attributes, or supernatural powers. It has, however, contributed to the many stories of a lone survivor of some great calamity coming back to carve a bloody streak through Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-08-2017, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T06:32:47-07:00","id":1126282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1126274#post1126274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the target has lost everything - they have no gods, no family, and no home - and they sift through the ashes of their home, they will find a mundane iron, steel, or bronze sword. If they lose it, they will shortly after find another one. As long as they possess any sword, they can deal lethal damage even to creatures that would normally be immune. Also, If they did not have at least three dots in the Melee Ability already, they gain up to that amount. These blessings last as long as the target lives.<br /> <br /> This ritual does not confer any other Abilities, Attributes, or supernatural powers. It has, however, contributed to the many stories of a lone survivor of some great calamity coming back to carve a bloody streak through Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really loved your write-up, but I feel it'd be more poignant if, when the thaumaturge finds the sword amidst the ashes of their home, they can either take it or leave it where it is. If they take it, all well and good, but if they leave it, no thaumaturgical power. Not this anyway. You had your chance at wreaking vengeance, you let it pass, done, see ya and buh-bye. Also, I wouldn't give them extra dots in Melee - the power to actually wound immaterial spirits is already pretty good for Thaumaturgy, and although the conditions required to get this power are absolutely awful and pretty specific, any PC could satisfy them with just a couple lines of background (maybe I'm underestimating Thaumaturgy's potential power, or I'm missing something. Apologies in that case).<br /> <br /> A final nitpick - I find that the many stories about lone survivors coming back to kick ass and take names might be easily more inspired by, well, Exaltation. Lunars, Abyssals and Infernals are the ones that seem more appropriate to me; and the character concept sounds more like something of the magnitude of an Exaltation than a simple thaumaturgical ritual. But again, that's just me being terminally anal retentive.<br /> <br /> Very cool power!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:31:02-07:00","id":1126298,"title":"","content":"I adapted a low-end Artifact from previous editions to a thaumaturgy ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctify the Waters (\u2022)</b><br /> Pearl divers in the West sometimes discover this rare talent. By placing a pearl worth Resources \u2022\u2022 or greater into a vessel of water, the thaumaturgist may spend a Willpower to render its contents drinkable, no matter how salty or fouled it is. The water will remain fresh and drinkable as long as the pearl remains, unless the water is befouled with magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:19:18-07:00","id":1126332,"title":"","content":"Just had this silly idea, inspired by omnipresence of identical-looking quest-giver/healer sisters in a number of videogames (nurse Joy &amp; officer Jenny being the ur-examples that actually joke with it), of a thaumaturgical ritual: Home Is Where the Heart Is.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it would work like those magical keys that can turn a door into a passage to Malfeas, but instead leads you to the home of a relative, or alternatively, a loved one (positive intimacy). How does that sound to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T09:34:59-07:00","id":1126334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1126282#post1126282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really loved your write-up, but I feel it'd be more poignant if, when the thaumaturge finds the sword amidst the ashes of their home, they can either take it or leave it where it is. If they take it, all well and good, but if they leave it, no thaumaturgical power. Not this anyway. You had your chance at wreaking vengeance, you let it pass, done, see ya and buh-bye. Also, I wouldn't give them extra dots in Melee - the power to actually wound immaterial spirits is already pretty good for Thaumaturgy, and although the conditions required to get this power are absolutely awful and pretty specific, any PC could satisfy them with just a couple lines of background (maybe I'm underestimating Thaumaturgy's potential power, or I'm missing something. Apologies in that case).<br /> <br /> A final nitpick - I find that the many stories about lone survivors coming back to kick ass and take names might be easily more inspired by, well, Exaltation. Lunars, Abyssals and Infernals are the ones that seem more appropriate to me; and the character concept sounds more like something of the magnitude of an Exaltation than a simple thaumaturgical ritual. But again, that's just me being terminally anal retentive.<br /> <br /> Very cool power!</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, this is inspired by a book, in which characters who come from this kind of traumatic background describe how using a sword felt... strangely intuitive, even if they'd never held one before. Out of nowhere, they gained a talent for violence that put them above many others. I figure if you've got an ST who'd be willing to give a player character extra Ability dots for a good backstory, the ritual is irrelevant. If you don't have such a permissive ST, the ritual won't be allowed anyway, so what does it matter?<br /> <br /> TBH, I don't see this ritual as one that a player would see used on their own characters... although a particularly sadistic PC might use it on others. If your character concept involves being able to wield swords and fight spirits, there are other ways to reach that goal that don't require you to be a murderhobo by default.<br /> <br /> As for revenge-comebacks - yes, the Exalted do it too. But every kind of Exalt you named can come from a much more diverse range of backgrounds than &quot;Nay-theist homeless orphan.&quot; I don't see why they should be the only ones to get perks for dramatic trauma. Besides, the &quot;no gods&quot; requirement clashes with the basic premise of Exaltation, which is explicitly power that came from a god.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1126332#post1126332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just had this silly idea, inspired by omnipresence of identical-looking quest-giver/healer sisters in a number of videogames (nurse Joy &amp; officer Jenny being the ur-examples that actually joke with it), of a thaumaturgical ritual: Home Is Where the Heart Is.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it would work like those magical keys that can turn a door into a passage to Malfeas, but instead leads you to the home of a relative, or alternatively, a loved one (positive intimacy). How does that sound to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty powerful. If you can turn any door into a teleport to a specific place, that's potentially pretty broken. Moreso if you can go back the way you came.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a way to run into the same-ish friendly face everywhere you go, it might be simpler to have a charm that summons the same or a similar friendly spirit along with their workshop/office/store/etc. Or, maybe the &quot;home&quot; you are going to exists in Elsewhere, so you can travel there from anywhere but not travel on to anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 08-08-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T10:20:56-07:00","id":1126351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1126334#post1126334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, this is inspired by a book, in which characters who come from this kind of traumatic background describe how using a sword felt... strangely intuitive, even if they'd never held one before. Out of nowhere, they gained a talent for violence that put them above many others. I figure if you've got an ST who'd be willing to give a player character extra Ability dots for a good backstory, the ritual is irrelevant. If you don't have such a permissive ST, the ritual won't be allowed anyway, so what does it matter?<br /> <br /> TBH, I don't see this ritual as one that a player would see used on their own characters... although a particularly sadistic PC might use it on others. If your character concept involves being able to wield swords and fight spirits, there are other ways to reach that goal that don't require you to be a murderhobo by default.<br /> <br /> As for revenge-comebacks - yes, the Exalted do it too. But every kind of Exalt you named can come from a much more diverse range of backgrounds than &quot;Nay-theist homeless orphan.&quot; I don't see why they should be the only ones to get perks for dramatic trauma. Besides, the &quot;no gods&quot; requirement clashes with the basic premise of Exaltation, which is explicitly power that came from a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well technically Abyssals and Infernals aren't receiving their Exaltations from gods, but I get what you mean, and I see how it's a specific niche not covered by &quot;normal&quot; Exaltations. And yeah, actually 3 points of Melee won't break any campaign, and few characters will actually have a use for them anyways...<br /> <br /> I later read the rituals you adapted from Unknown Armies (love that game!) and they're made of awesome. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar298_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"298\" data-vbnamecard=\"298\">Jen</a>'s too. Never thought Ex3 thaumaturgy could be so cool. Thumbs up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T11:57:30-07:00","id":1126399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1126334#post1126334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds pretty powerful. If you can turn any door into a teleport to a specific place, that's potentially pretty broken. Moreso if you can go back the way you came.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would require adjustment for certain (doesn't even have the, but main idea is to go from a place that counts as <b>home</b> to the character to the house of a relative/loved one by use of the ritual in an appropriate door/arch, so the <i>Home Is Where the <b>Heart</b> Is</i> name's reason in the first place.<br /> <br /> As implied previously, intimacies would be a requirement (&quot;family&quot; as a whole being covered with one too, as a sort of special case/exception possibly), what can be a blessing and curse at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T13:54:41-07:00","id":1126439,"title":"","content":"Put stones in a pot cook them with sticks, and you have a nourishing broth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T12:33:45-07:00","id":1232467,"title":"","content":"<b>Flowers of the Sun (O)</b><br /> One who knows this ritual can pick a light-coloured flower - white, yellow or pale pink at the darkest - and whisper certain words over it (which one well-versed in ancient dialects of Old Realm might recognize as 'For your smile') before holding it up to present to the sun. If done right, the sun seems to brighten for the merest fraction of a moment and the flower answers, transforming into a five-petalled blossom of golden hue. It will wither like any other picked flower, but while it remains verdant it will glow like a candle in darkness and exudes a comforting warmth.<br /> <br /> This gift appears occasionally among the children of An-Teng, particularly those who live in the highlands or close to the mountain atop which the Golden Lord dwells. Ancient tales say that it was first taught to a young girl in ancient days by a great hero who wished to see her smile. The Tengese regard those children who know this ritual as blessed by the Golden Lord and often send them to serve in the priesthood. The household which keeps a sun-flower in its ancestral shrine is considered to be under an auspice of good fortune.<br /> <br /> <b>Whispers Entrusted to the Waters (OO)</b><br /> A thaumaturge who knows this ritual knows the way of folding a message written on leaves or paper into a minute boat. She then whispers the name of the intended recipient into the little craft and sets it upon the waters of a river, canal, lake or other non-sea body of water, accompanied by a small offering of her own blood. So long as the recipient visits the body of water sometime in the next season they will unerringly receive the conveyed message, provided that they are downstream if the body of water is a flowing one.<br /> <br /> This ritual appears throughout Creation in those who live on lakesides, riverbanks or along other waterways, most often to those in whose destiny is written some great destiny of love and separation. Many are the romantic legends in which lovers exchange messages via rivers, as are tragedies where a beloved recieves news of their love's death via a leaf-boat buoyed on flowing waters and stained with life-blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Tasting the Storm (O)</b><br /> When you live on an island or ply the waves, knowing when a storm is coming is essential knowledge, and for this reason those born with the gift of tasting storm-winds from afar are greatly valued across the West, where they are most often born, and beyond.<br /> <br /> A storm-taster may sifts the air unconsciously throughout the day with a (Perception + Occult) roll, which is rolled upon waking, dawn or at some other early point in the day when the thaumaturge is exposed to the sky. For each success, he may taste a storm on its way one day ahead of its arrival by a metallic tang to the air. The storm-taster isn't aware of making an effort to taste the air - it's just a part of how he is. If he tastes a storm on the way, he may roll again against a Difficulty of 2 to ascertain the rough direction from which the storm will approach. He may only do so once per day, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 07-06-2018, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T09:28:47-07:00","id":1232639,"title":"","content":"How about a ritual that lets you boil water by praying at it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T09:31:58-07:00","id":1232640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1232639#post1232639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a ritual that lets you boil water by praying at it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds a little... straightforward to me. Too much like just a D&amp;D-style cantrip. Any ideas for how to spice it up a little? Maybe there's some other ritual which just happens to be very useful for boiling water. Like maybe something to invoke the traces of fire-Essence in volcanic rock, heating it - which if you put it in a pot conveniently allows you to boil water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T09:42:36-07:00","id":1232644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1232640#post1232640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds a little... straightforward to me. Too much like just a D&amp;D-style cantrip. Any ideas for how to spice it up a little? Maybe there's some other ritual which just happens to be very useful for boiling water. Like maybe something to invoke the traces of fire-Essence in volcanic rock, heating it - which if you put it in a pot conveniently allows you to boil water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe take pieces of wood, arrange them in a shape around the pot, and then the water starts boiling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T09:57:28-07:00","id":1232646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1232644#post1232644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe take pieces of wood, arrange them in a shape around the pot, and then the water starts boiling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's to do with the container in which you boil the water? Maybe the ritualist knows a string of elegant but meaningless symbols which, if inscribed in a full circle around a container (e.g. a teapot, a cauldron etc) cause any water within to boil if a finger is wetted with the contents and traced over the ring? I kind of like the idea of the latter part of the ritual being able to be done by anyone, as it lets me make a potter NPC who makes a small fortune by making teapots that heat themselves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This totally isn't so I have backstory for why a random kingdom has a version of the tea ceremony, due to the reoccurrence of this ritual throughout its history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 07-05-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T09:08:51-07:00","id":1235274,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Name-Bound Venom (OO)</b></u><br /> A ritual that is the secret founding-technique of more than one order of assassins, Name-Bound Venom allows one who knows it to trace a specific name in Old Realm a thousand times upon the surface of a liquid (which does not have to be poisonous, despite the name). A brew thus prepared will impart any effect it might have only upon one who bears the name that has been worked into the liquid. The liquid will affect any who consider that name to be their own, irrespective of whether or not they are the one whom the venom was intended for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T14:36:41-07:00","id":1244928,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any ideas for an Oramaic-flavoured Thaumaturgy ritual, or something that interacts somehow with the Beyond?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T14:45:13-07:00","id":1244929,"title":"","content":"The latter seems like something way above the pay grade of Thaumaturgy to me. I'm not sure Oramus or Luna would bestow powers dealing with it to their chosen, nevermind regular folks in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T14:55:12-07:00","id":1244931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/812137-ex3-thaumaturgy-rituals?p=1244929#post1244929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter seems like something way above the pay grade of Thaumaturgy to me. I'm not sure Oramus or Luna would bestow powers dealing with it to their chosen, nevermind regular folks in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean anything particularly direct. I'm trying to represent a person who saw Things Man Should Not Know and learned some secret from that, but I'm not sure what it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T15:35:15-07:00","id":1244942,"title":"","content":"Maybe some minor prophecy and danger sense, but it has the possibility of being wildly wrong, so you end up screaming at nothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}